372d-b7fa-5167-9fa9-2256ded10162'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Kaluuya won for his performance as the Black Panther leader Fred Hampton in “Judas and the Black Messiah,” while Chadwick Boseman was awarded a posthumous Globe for his role in “Ma Rainey’s Black Bottom.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/28/movies/daniel-kaluuya-john-boyega.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Kaluuya won for his performance as the Black Panther leader Fred Hampton in “Judas and the Black Messiah,” while Chadwick Boseman was awarded a posthumous Globe for his role in “Ma Rainey’s Black Bottom.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As soon as nominations were announced on Feb. 3, the foreign press association was harshly criticized for overlooking films with mostly Black casts, including Spike Lee’s “Da 5 Bloods.” But the ceremony began with back-to-back honors for Black actors. The night’s first winner was Daniel Kaluuya, for best supporting actor for his performance as the Black Panther leader Fred Hampton in “Judas and the Black Messiah.” John Boyega then won best supporting actor in a TV series for playing a police officer in Amazon’s “Small Axe.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/28/arts/28golden-globes-briefing-black-artists-boyega/merlin_184406538_5ab88c81-07b3-4aa8-8940-8830c255f812-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/02/28/arts/28golden-globes-briefing-black-artists-boyega/merlin_184406538_5ab88c81-07b3-4aa8-8940-8830c255f812-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/28/arts/28golden-globes-briefing-black-artists-boyega/merlin_184406538_5ab88c81-07b3-4aa8-8940-8830c255f812-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy'