lue': 'Boylan, Lindsey (1984- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T09:48:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mihir Zaveri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mihir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zaveri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/263b39ee-0934-5eb9-bd7a-675cdc7b598b', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/263b39ee-0934-5eb9-bd7a-675cdc7b598b'}, {'abstract': 'Amid deeply moving moments (like the speech by Chadwick Boseman’s widow), there were technical difficulties and the strange sight of long-distance hosts pretending to be on the same stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/movies/best-worst-golden-globes.html', 'snippet': 'Amid deeply moving moments (like the speech by Chadwick Boseman’s widow), there were technical difficulties and the strange sight of long-distance hosts pretending to be on the same stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a Golden Globes like no other, for better (the winners’ backdrops!) and worse (the technical glitches!). The challenges of putting on an awards ceremony in the midst of a pandemic were evident in ways large and small on Sunday night, while a series of exposés about the Hollywood Foreign Press Association, the group that hands out the awards, set the tone for the show. Here are the evening’s highs and lows as we saw them. — Stephanie Goodman', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/01/business/01globes-best-worst-hosts/merlin_184406544_d4391775-8d37-48c8-8149-51855af9268f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleL