'subject', 'value': 'Actors and Actresses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boseman, Chadwick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Day, Andra (1984- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Docter, Pete', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaluuya, Daniel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Laverne', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Jodie', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poehler, Amy', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhao, Chloe', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fey, Tina', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T09:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c987237d-cea6-5313-844f-94e4290e8928', 'word_count': 1592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c987237d-cea6-5313-844f-94e4290e8928'}, {'abstract': 'What advice would you give to a peer who is struggling with schoolwork and feeling like catching up is impossible?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/learning/how-should-parents-support-a-student-who-has-fallen-behind-in-school.html', 'snippet': 'What advice would you give to a peer who is struggling with schoolwork and feeling like catching up is impossible?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Try to name as many reasons as you can why a student might fall behind in schoolwork — reasons that are particularly relevant to the challenges of the current school year. Why can it be difficult to pull oneself out of a downward academic spiral or “homework hole”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/well/26Well-teen-school/26Well-teen-school-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/02/26/well/26Well-teen-school/26Well-teen-school-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/well/26Well-teen-school/26Well-teen-school-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/well/26Well-teen-school/26Well-teen-school-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1750, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/well/26Well-teen-school/26Well-teen-school-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/02/26/well/26Well-teen-school/26Well-teen-school-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/well/26Well-teen-school/26Well-teen-school-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Should Parents Support a Student Who Has Fallen Behind in School?', 'kicker': 'student opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/599dbaef-ebb0-5fa0-897f-cdede5a3a10f', 'word_count': 1634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/599dbaef-ebb0-5fa0-897f-cdede5a3a10f'}, {'abstract': 'The crowdfunding platform helps people pay their rent and medical bills. Its chief executive, Tim Cadogan, says it was never meant to be a social safety net.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/opinion/sway-kara-swisher-tim-cadogan.html', 'snippet': 'The crowdfunding platform helps people pay their rent and medical bills. Its chief executive, Tim Cadogan, says it was never meant to be a social safety net.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House has just passed a $1.9 trillion stimulus bill which is now pending Senate approval. GoFundMe C.E.O. Tim Cadogan hopes the package will alleviate some of the economic pain of the pandemic. Activity on his crowdfunding platform has surged in the wake of Covid-19, with users turning to GoFundMe to help pay for everything from rent to funeral services. Cadogan would rather that the government — not his company — play this role. “This is a war against a virus,” he says. “If this were a war against another country at this scale, it would be no question what we would do, right? We would mobilize our society to defeat it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/opinion/01sway-cadogan-image/01sway-cadogan-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/03/opinion/01sway-cadogan-image/01sway-cadogan-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/opinion/01sway-cadogan-image/01sway-cadogan-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/opinion/01sway-cadogan-image/01sway-cadogan-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1619, 'width': 1619, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/opinion/01sway-cadogan-image/01sway-cadogan-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/03/opinion/01sway-cadogan-image/01sway-cadogan-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/opinion/01sway-cadogan-image/01sway-cadogan-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If Government Did Its Job We Might Not Need GoFundMe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdfunding (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stimulus (Economic)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GoFundMe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cadogan, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kara Swisher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swisher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/669c324f-8883-5330-9504-3774218f91d5', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/669c324f-8883-5330-9504-3774218f91d5'}, {'abstract': 'If you’ve been fortunate enough to put away some cash, here are a few ideas on what to do with it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/style/money-advice-pandemic-savings.html', 'snippet': 'If you’ve been fortunate enough to put away some cash, here are a few ideas on what to do with it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The uneven economic recovery in the U.S. is a cruel outcome of the pandemic and systematic inequality. Millions of Americans remain unemployed, and the systems we have in place to help have failed many of them. But if you squint, there is a silver lining for some: More Americans have been able to save money and pay off debt since lockdowns across the country have meant less travel, less entertainment and less dining out.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/fashion/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/17/fashion/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/fashion/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/fashion/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/fashion/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/17/fashion/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/fashion/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art/15SLNEWSLETTER-Money-Art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So You Saved a Little Money This Past Year. Now What?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here to Help; So You Saved a Little Money This Past Year. Now What?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Herrera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herrera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ecc5d14-8555-5c95-85e8-677d4706cc99', 'word_count': 1186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ecc5d14-8555-5c95-85e8-677d4706cc99'}, {'abstract': 'Autism spectrum disorder is often suspected when young children stand out as being different from their peers. That can be much harder in this isolated time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/well/family/diagnosing-autism-in-the-pandemic.html', 'snippet': 'Autism spectrum disorder is often suspected when young children stand out as being different from their peers. That can be much harder in this isolated time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We talk often in pediatrics about the importance of early identification and early treatment of autism spectrum disorder, with its hallmark issues of social communication problems and restricted repetitive behavior patterns. “Early” means paying particularly close attention to the behavior and development of children between ages 1 and 3, and checking in with their parents about any concerns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/28/well/00well-autism-diagnosis/00well-autism-diagnosis-articleLarge.png', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/02/28/well/00well-autism-diagnosis/00well-autism-diagnosis-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/28/well/00well-autism-diagnosis/00well-autism-diagnosis-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/28/well/00well-autism-diagnosis/00well-autism-diagnosis-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/28/well/00well-autism-diagnosis/00well-autism-diagnosis