chocolates are sold. The kitchen is visible behind the counter and the chocolates are available nationwide. The fillings are uncommon, but before pistachio-saffron caramel or chai latte hits your tongue, you have to appreciate the finesse of the silky, 72-percent dark chocolate shell that enrobes each one. They’re modest, bite-size and sell for $3 to $3.25 each. They’re also assembled in preset or custom assortments in the shop or to order online, $14 to $55 plus shipping.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-chocolate/01Burner-chocolate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-chocolate/01Burner-chocolate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-chocolate/01Burner-chocolate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-chocolate/01Burner-chocolate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-chocolate/01Burner-chocolate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-chocolate/01Burner-chocolate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-chocolate/01Burner-chocolate-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vegan Chocolates Filled With Delights', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Nibble: Vegan Chocolates  Filled With Delights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veganism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T22:44:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1af3b510-c101-52da-ab07-345bba9c0d29', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1af3b510-c101-52da-ab07-345bba9c0d29'}, {'abstract': '“American Cider” looks at the history of the beverage, and it discusses how it is made, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/dining/american-cider-book.html', 'snippet': '“American Cider” looks at the history of the beverage, and it discusses how it is made, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dan Pucci and Craig Cavallo, the authors of the comprehensive new book  “American Cider,” say the drink that sustained colonial America is having a renaissance. They documented the resurgence of cider mills across the country, a 100-fold increase since 1991. Their thumbnail history of cider traces it from the Old World, around the time of Christ. This serious but easygoing book points out that ciders tend to be a local quaff unlike wine, which always had an international market. The authors discuss the many different apples (in the 19th century there were 1,000 varieties growing in the United States), which ones are suited for cider, how cider is made and even the geology of the land, as they survey ciders in eight regions across the country.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-book/01Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-book/01Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 911}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-book/01Burner-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-book/01Burner-book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1349, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-book/01Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-book/01Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-book/01Burner-book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Book Covers the Hard Stuff', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Peruse: This Book Covers The Hard Stuff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cider', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T22:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79c40039-5732-511e-95b0-5e177a8233cc', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79c40039-5732-511e-95b0-5e177a8233cc'}, {'abstract': 'People who convert in Israel to Reform or Conservative Judaism have a right to citizenship, the Supreme Court ruled, chipping at the power of Orthodox authorities that see them as non-Jewish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/world/middleeast/israel-jewish-converts-citizenship.html', 'snippet': 'People who convert in Israel to Reform or Conservative Judaism have a right to citizenship, the Supreme Court ruled, chipping at the power of Orthodox authorities that see them as non-Jewish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The question of who is and isn’t a Jew has always been a subject of debate within Israel. Since the state was founded, the government has largely deferred to Orthodox Jewish authorities, who do not view converts to more liberal forms of Judaism as Jewish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/01/world/01israel-jews-2-promo/merlin_184440636_e46d4a31-b316-4d6e-87f6-5cac223d1a9c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/01/world/01israel-jews-2-promo/merlin_184440636_e46d4a31-b316-4d6e-87f6-5cac223d1a9c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/01/world/01israel-jews-2-promo/merlin_184440636_e46d4a31-b316-4d6e-87f6-5cac223d1a9c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/01/world/01israel-jews-2-promo/merlin_184440636_e46d4a31-b316-4d6e-87f6-5cac223d1a9c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/01/world/01israel-jews-2-promo/01israel-jews-2-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/01/world/01israel-jews-2-promo/01israel-jews-2-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/01/world/01israel-jews-2-promo/01israel-jews-2-promo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli Court Says Converts to Non-Orthodox Judaism Can Claim Citizenship', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ruling in Israel Broadens View Of Which Jews Can Be Citizens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Orthodox Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T22:49:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Kingsley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kingsley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b37444e-a419-5bb4-b7f9-d57d257100a2', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b37444e-a419-5bb4-b7f9-d57d257100a2'}, {'abstract': 'Maui Nui sells various cuts from Axis deer, and the harvest helps combat erosion that has affected the island’s coral reefs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/dining/maui-nui-venison.html', 'snippet': 'Maui Nui sells various cuts from Axis deer, and the harvest helps combat erosion that has affected the island’s coral reefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Areas across the country, even some suburbs, have to deal with growing herds of often unwelcome deer. Count Maui, in Hawaii, among them. Axis deer, an Asian breed, were introduced for hunting in the mid-1900s, and they still attract the sharp-shooting crowd. But as their numbers have grown to the tens of thousands, the deer are also considered to be an invasive menace, not just on the roads, but for the way they denude the landscape of vegetation, causing erosion and water runoffs that can damage coral reefs. Maui Nui, a new company, is now turning them into dinner. Across the island, it harvests wild deer at night so the animals are supposedly less stressed and uses a mobile slaughtering facility. Now various cuts of venison, frozen, in preset combinations that include succulent racks, medallions, strip loins, stew meat for a nice braise and ground venison can be shipped to customers across the United States. The meat is mild-tasting, slightly beefy and tender. It’s also very lean, so add some slab bacon to your stew and plenty of olive oil to the ragù. A four-chop rack serving two will take about 20 minutes at 425 degrees for medium-rare. The company’s bone broth is delicious.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-venison/01Burner-venison-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-venison/01Burner-venison-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-venison/01Burner-venison-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-venison/01Burner-venison-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-venison/01Burner-venison-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-venison/01Burner-venison-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-venison/01Burner-venison-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venison All the Way From Hawaii', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Prepare: Cuts of Venison  Courtesy of Hawaii', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venison', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maui (Hawaii)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T22:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ea800ed-6c0c-5314-9a06-29f7c9d30817', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ea800ed-6c0c-5314-9a06-29f7c9d30817'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Mitchel London has opened a takeaway spot named for his business partner’s mother, Twiggy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/dining/twiggy-to-go-mitchel-london.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Mitchel London has opened a takeaway spot named for his business partner’s mother, Twiggy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around the beginning of the pandemic, the chef and caterer Mitchel London began offering deliveries of prepared food from a kitchen in TriBeCa. It was a holding pattern that he and his business partner, Thomas Mikolasko, decided on while finishing a restaurant they planned in the space. Now, with the restaurant project postponed, they have opened an inviting retail shop named Twiggy — after Mr. Mikolasko’s mother’s nickname — in the front of that space. The store has a bright display of quiches, thick rustic pizzas, bright green beans, roasted endives, crisp chiplike potatoes, several iterations of chicken (including fried), meat loaf and some salads, all offered on a rotating basis. There are also sensational pastries, including a deeply burnished tarte Tatin, ethereal lemon meringue cake and feathery raspberry mille-feuille. In addition to pickup at the store, food can be ordered for delivery to only Manhattan, for now.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-Store/01Burner-Store-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-Store/01Burner-Store-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-Store/01Burner-Store-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-Store/01Burner-Store-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-Store/01Burner-Store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-Store/01Burner-Store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/01Burner-Store/01Burner-Store-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Caterer Opens a To-Go Operation in TriBeCa', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Dine: A Caterer Opens A To-Go Spot in TriBeCa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 