 support, but Washington remains bitterly divided on the details.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/business/infrastructure-biden-stimulus.html', 'snippet': 'Strengthening the country’s highways, bridges and broadband networks has broad popular support, but Washington remains bitterly divided on the details.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Biden’s two immediate predecessors had ambitious goals to rebuild the country’s infrastructure, but both left office having made little progress in fixing the nation’s bridges, roads, pipes and broadband. President Donald J. Trump announced so many meaningless infrastructure weeks that the term became a running joke of his administration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/19/us/politics/00DC-INFRASTRUCTURE1/merlin_183952494_1594a920-e377-4258-8ba6-7e8c78e30d29-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/02/19/us/politics/00DC-INFRASTRUCTURE1/merlin_183952494_1594a920-e377-4258-8ba6-7e8c78e30d29-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/19/us/politics/00DC-INFRASTRUCTURE1/merlin_183952494_1594a920-e377-4258-8ba6-7e8c78e30d29-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/19/us/politics/00DC-INFRASTRUCTURE1/merlin_183952494_1594a920-e377-4258-8ba6-7e8c78e30d29-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/19/us/politics/00DC-INFRASTRUCTURE1/merlin_183952494_1594a920-e377-4258-8ba6-7e8c78e30d29-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/02/19/us/politics/00DC-INFRASTRUCTURE1/merlin_183952494_1594a920-e377-4258-8ba6-7e8c78e30d29-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/19/us/politics/00DC-INFRASTRUCTURE1/merlin_183952494_1594a920-e377-4258-8ba6-7e8c78e30d29-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Stimulus, Biden to Tackle Another Politically Tricky Issue: Infrastructure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biden’s Infrastructure Package May Be Trickier Than Aid Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stimulus (Economic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security Act (2020)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buttigieg, Pete (1982- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-01T22:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Karni and Jim Tankersley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tankersley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dabf4f9e-c52c-5558-aca2-269cf7454638', 'word_count': 1800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dabf4f9e-c52c-5558-aca2-269cf7454638'}, {'abstract': 'Monique Péan’s sculptures and fine jewelry designs are meditations on deep time and the origins of humanity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/t-magazine/monique-pean-sculpture-jewelry.html', 'snippet': 'Monique Péan’s sculptures and fine jewelry designs are meditations on deep time and the origins of humanity.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I wish you were here in person so I could put the joint bone in your hand.” The artist and designer Monique Péan and I are on a Zoom call, and she’s sitting at the worktable of her Manhattan studio cradling a softball-size hunk of what, on first glance, looks like an ordinary rock. In fact, it is from an Ichthyosaurus, a marine reptile that lived during the Mesozoic Era, which means it could be as much as 250 million years old. “I got this as a 35th birthday present to myself,” says Péan, now 39. As the image on my screen resolves, one end of the fossil, polished to a mirror finish, reveals flecks of white, peach, bright red and blue. Up close, they resemble stars against the night sky. “It’s almost like a world unto itself,” she says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/25/t-magazine/25tmag-monique-pean-slide-XEO1-copy/25tmag-monique-pean-slide-XEO1-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'wi