ut the photographer Gordon Parks misidentified a memoir by Mr. Parks and described incorrectly the sequence of events in a recollection in the book. The memoir is “A Hungry Heart,” not “Voices in the Mirror”; and he photographed a gown whose color reminded him of the blood of a murdered gang member after he had photographed the gang member, not before. The article also misidentified the setting of a photograph Mr. Parks took in 1956. It was at a theater in Mobile, Ala., not a department store (Mr. Parks titled the work “Department Store”). And the article, using information from the Gordon Parks Foundation, misstated the year he bought his first camera. It was 1938, not 1937.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: March 4, 2021', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-03-04T03:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/8309737f-7177-5f7a-87c4-6034b8146c6e', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8309737f-7177-5f7a-87c4-6034b8146c6e'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, March 4, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/03/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-biden-denounces-states-for-lifting-orders-on-masks.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, March 4, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The light’s there at the very end of the tunnel, and now we’ve made the tunnel longer. It’s foolish. It’s beyond foolish.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Biden Denounces States for Lifting Orders on Masks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the 