title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/340067b2-990e-5b9c-8e95-24b0cf30cf05', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/340067b2-990e-5b9c-8e95-24b0cf30cf05'}, {'abstract': 'Carl Phillips turns loss into more than another sad song, into sorrow, which feels heavier and seems to matter more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/magazine/poem-pale-colors-in-a-tall-field.html', 'snippet': 'Carl Phillips turns loss into more than another sad song, into sorrow, which feels heavier and seems to matter more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Phillips turns the syntax of a sentence into something like the chords of a bagpipe. To the unfamiliar, the beauty of it feels strange. Phillips turns loss into more than another sad song, into sorrow, which feels heavier and seems to matter more. I might be wrong about bagpipes and Phillips’s poetry and how they each remind me of Luther Vandross. But they do. And this one reminds me that I, too, have “reached that point in my own life/where there’s so much I’d rather not remember.” There is sorrow in admitting that. But a bit of joy in being able to say it aloud. Selected by Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-poem/07mag-poem-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-poem/07mag-poem-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-poem/07mag-poem-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-poem/07mag-poem-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1094, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-poem/07mag-poem-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-poem/07mag-poem-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-poem/07mag-poem-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Pale Colors in a Tall Field', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Carl (1959- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-04T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Phillips and Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phillips', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Reginald', 'middlename': 'Dwayne', 'lastname': 'Betts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8b10cc4-2aaa-5f3a-82a1-2d2ed957be1b', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8b10cc4-2aaa-5f3a-82a1-2d2ed957be1b'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of tests turned up nothing. Then a specialist had a theory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/magazine/myasthenia-gravis-mg-diagnosis.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens of tests turned up nothing. Then a specialist had a theory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The voice on the phone was kind but firm: “You need to go to the emergency room. Now.” Her morning was going to be busy, replied the 68-year-old woman, and she didn’t feel well. Could she go later today or maybe tomorrow? No, said Dr. Benison Keung, her neurologist. She needed to go now; it was important. As she hung up the phone, tears blurred the woman’s already bad vision. She’d been worried for a while; now she was terrified. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-Diagnosis-1/07mag-Diagnosis-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-Diagnosis-1/07mag-Diagnosis-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 460}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-Diagnosis-1/07mag-Diagnosis-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-Diagnosis-1/07mag-Diagnosis-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1570, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-Diagnosis-1/07mag-Diagnosis-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-Diagnosis-1/07mag-Diagnosis-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-Diagnosis-1/07mag-Diagnosis-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Her Eyelid Drooped and She Kept Getting Weaker. What Was Going On?', 'kicker': 'Diagnosis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immune System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-04T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4372c942-831a-589a-9c48-61e91725bf5f', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4372c942-831a-589a-9c48-61e91725bf5f'}, {'abstract': 'Abrams helped win major Democratic victories in Georgia, the right is retaliating and it’s getting personal. But Abrams says she doesn’t mind; it’s all about the long game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/opinion/sway-kara-swisher-stacey-abrams.html', 'snippet': 'Abrams helped win major Democratic victories in Georgia, the right is retaliating and it’s getting personal. But Abrams says she doesn’t mind; it’s all about the long game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stacey Abrams’s focus on expanding voter turnout and turning Georgia blue paid off this year when Jon Ossoff and Raphael Warnock both flipped Senate seats, handing Democrats a slim majority in Congress. Republicans ar