3ec74a', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d6b755d-7d8d-54e3-af7d-f464ba3ec74a'}, {'abstract': 'A widow welcomes a pregnant stranger into her home in this sentimental story mostly told unsentimentally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/movies/adam-review.html', 'snippet': 'A widow welcomes a pregnant stranger into her home in this sentimental story mostly told unsentimentally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Maryam Touzani’s “Adam,” certain stylistic choices — a muted palette, the absence of a melodramatic score, hand-held camerawork — help temper sentimentality with verisimilitude. The movie tells a story of kindness given and returned. It opens with Samia (Nisrin Erradi) seeking a job as a hairdresser, and then as a maid, or really as anything. As a pregnant woman alone in Casablanca, she needs work and a place to stay — and encounters mainly indifference and judgment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/adam1/merlin_184222869_41346bbf-e129-4246-8e6e-bc5878af1d64-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/adam1/merlin_184222869_41346bbf-e129-4246-8e6e-bc5878af1d64-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/adam1/merlin_184222869_41346bbf-e129-4246-8e6e-bc5878af1d64-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/adam1/merlin_184222869_41346bbf-e129-4246-8e6e-bc5878af1d64-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1998, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/adam1/adam1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/adam1/adam1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/adam1/adam1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Adam’ Review: Beginning of a Beautiful Friendship', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Adam (2021) (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Touzani, Maryam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-04T12:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/50d56631-58b7-5985-9154-fd09741b6499', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50d56631-58b7-5985-9154-fd09741b6499'}, {'abstract': 'An animal trainer turned activist strives to end sea mammal captivity in this documentary that could use a sharper frame on its subject.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/movies/the-walrus-and-the-whistleblower-review.html', 'snippet': 'An animal trainer turned activist strives to end sea mammal captivity in this documentary that could use a sharper frame on its subject.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Marineland, the sprawling aquatic park in Niagara Falls, Ontario, lives a walrus named Smooshi. Concerns for the sea mammal’s well-being form the core of the documentary “The Walrus and the Whistleblower,” which follows the former trainer Phil Demers’s fight to free Smooshi from her captivity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/06/arts/walrus1/walrus1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/06/arts/walrus1/walrus1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/06/arts/walrus1/walrus1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/06/arts/walrus1/walrus1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/06/arts/walrus1/walrus1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/06/arts/walrus1/walrus1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/06/arts/walrus1/walrus1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Walrus and the Whistleblower’ Review: The Fight to Free a Friend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Are All Together: An Aquatic Bond', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Walrus and the Whistleblower (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bibeau, Nathalie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-04T12:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalia Winkelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winkelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/541d55b1-3656-53b8-86b9-d4e095b88c3b', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/541d55b1-3656-53b8-86b9-d4e095b88c3b'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary offers a dry, rote introduction to a designer who became a key figure in the Arts and Crafts movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/movies/gustav-stickley-american-craftsman-review.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary offers a dry, rote introduction to a designer who became a key figure in the Arts and Crafts movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The documentary “Gustav Stickley: American Craftsman” offers an introduction to a designer (1858-1942) who became a crucial figure in the American Arts and Crafts movement. But the movie itself, directed by Herb Stratford, is so dull and unimaginative in its presentation — talking heads, an overused score that might as well have been downloaded from a free database — that it makes for an unfortunate match of subject matter and form.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/02/arts/gustav1/merlin_184259346_92db6081-2532-4