eported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4d8dbae-b10c-541c-a80b-14a3d3274550', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4d8dbae-b10c-541c-a80b-14a3d3274550'}, {'abstract': 'I lied about my sexuality to appease them. Now I’m in a bind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/style/coming-out-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'I lied about my sexuality to appease them. Now I’m in a bind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am a queer high school senior and the daughter of evangelical Christians. I have kept my sexuality secret from them. During the pandemic, I got lonely, so I started chatting on L.G.B.T.Q. message boards. Unfortunately, I was careless with my browser history. My mother saw it and freaked out. She made me swear I’m not a lesbian. I did. My parents are also making me talk to their minister every week. If I don’t, they say I will have to leave home. They also threatened not to help with college costs next year. (They’re not kidding.) So, now I’m lying to their minister too. I hate this! I like to think of myself as a good person. Should I come clean?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/soci