8+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sapna Maheshwari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sapna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maheshwari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8572407-b0a7-5a73-a1b6-18adbb896066', 'word_count': 1514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8572407-b0a7-5a73-a1b6-18adbb896066'}, {'abstract': 'More than 30 years later, Eddie Murphy and Arsenio Hall reunite for a return trip from Zamunda to New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/04/movies/coming-2-america-review.html', 'snippet': 'More than 30 years later, Eddie Murphy and Arsenio Hall reunite for a return trip from Zamunda to New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Breaking away from a lavish palace party meant to celebrate his engagement, Lavelle Junson (Jermaine Fowler), the newly minted crown prince of Zamunda, complains about the state of Hollywood filmmaking. He never says what kinds of movies he does like, but he’s vocal in his disdain for superhero spectacles and “sequels that nobody asked for.” Mirembe (Nomzamo Mbatha), his royal groomer and love interest, disagrees. Zamundan cinema isn’t so great, she says, and some of those sequels aren’t so bad.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/04/arts/04comingamerica1/04comingamerica1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/04/arts/04comingamerica1/04comingamerica1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/04/arts/04comingamerica1/04comingamerica1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 68