 did influencers become our moral authorities?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/05/opinion/influencers-glennon-doyle-instagram.html', 'snippet': 'How did influencers become our moral authorities?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Instagram, I follow 700 people, mostly women. One hundred of those women follow Glennon Doyle, whose memoir “Untamed” has been on the Times best-seller list for 51 weeks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Empty Religions of Instagram', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Influencers Are The New Televangelists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennial Generation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doyle, Glennon (1976- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-05T10:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leigh Stein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leigh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1929d08-fc66-51a7-9f1e-e546766c7167', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1929d08-fc66-51a7-9f1e-e546766c7167'}, {'abstract': 'A small yet aggressive segment of America refuses to accept that the country is made up of people from many different backgrounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/05/opinion/international-world/anti-asian-hate.html', 'snippet': 'A small yet aggressive segment of America refuses to accept that the country is made up of people from many different backgrounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pandemics fade. Racism does not. And when a president like Donald Trump unfairly blames an entire ethnic group for the coronavirus pandemic crisis, it can embolden discrimination and violence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/opinion/05Ramos1/merlin_184042620_6b8fcec3-d979-4289-a4f1-d831a3c0ba8a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/05/opinion/05Ramos1/merlin_184042620_6b8fcec3-d979-4289-a4f1-d831a3c0ba8a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/opinion/05Ramos1/merlin_184042620_6b8fcec3-d979-4289-a4f1-d831a3c0ba8a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/opinion/05Ramos1/merlin_184042620_6b8fcec3-d979-4289-a4f1-d831a3c0ba8a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/opinion/05Ramos1/05-amos1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/05/opinion/05Ramos1/05-amos1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/opinion/05Ramos1/05-amos1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headl