her you make a tater tot casserole, oden with homemade shrimp balls, or a comforting braciole.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/05/dining/what-to-cook-this-weekend.html', 'snippet': 'Set aside some time to cook, whether you make a tater tot casserole, oden with homemade shrimp balls, or a comforting braciole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Here’s some exciting news from the virtual headquarters of NYT Cooking: Our “No-Recipe Recipes” cookbook is now available for pre-order. (The book comes out on March 16, and, that evening, Melissa Clark and I will talk about it over the internet, if you’d like to join.) There’s an excerpt in The New York Times Magazine this weekend and, with it, a no-recipe recipe for a dinner of smothered pork chops with sautéed greens and lemony mashed potatoes (above). I hope you make that dinner this weekend and revel in the pleasures of improvisatory cooking. At this stage of the pandemic, it should come naturally. You’ve been cooking so much!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-eat/07mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-eat/07mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-eat/07mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/magazine/07mag-eat/07mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1541, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':