le', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Segal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Segal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1f0e6c2-5d44-5b93-872e-6ebf22e3d4e3', 'word_count': 2074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1f0e6c2-5d44-5b93-872e-6ebf22e3d4e3'}, {'abstract': 'A body mass index, or B.M.I., that indicates obesity can qualify someone for the Covid-19 vaccine, even if the measurement is outdated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/05/style/self-care/bmi-covid-vaccine.html', 'snippet': 'A body mass index, or B.M.I., that indicates obesity can qualify someone for the Covid-19 vaccine, even if the measurement is outdated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rebecca O’Neal didn’t believe she qualified for a Covid-19 vaccine. She had not realized that her turn had come. Last week, when she scrolled through the eligibility requirements for the state of New York, she noticed body mass index on the list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/fashion/03BMI-VACCINE/03BMI-VACCINE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/07/fashion/03BMI-VACCINE/03BMI-VACCINE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/fashion/03BMI-VACCINE/03BMI-VACCINE-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/07/fashion/03BMI-VACCINE/03BMI-VACCINE-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 155