al': 'By Ruth Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23fbedfa-0d4b-5ce1-b0a3-55b3735e0bca', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23fbedfa-0d4b-5ce1-b0a3-55b3735e0bca'}, {'abstract': 'The pope’s four-day trip is intended to nurture ties with Shiite Muslims and encourage a Christian population decimated by years of strife.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/05/world/middleeast/pope-francis-iraq-visit.html', 'snippet': 'The pope’s four-day trip is intended to nurture ties with Shiite Muslims and encourage a Christian population decimated by years of strife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Pope Francis made an audacious return to the world stage in the midst of the pandemic on Friday when he became the first leader of the Roman Catholic church to visit Iraq, seeking to help heal a nation uniquely wounded by violent sectarianism, foreign adventurism and the persecution of minority populations, including his own Christian flock.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Francis Begins Visit to Iraq, in ‘Duty to a Land Martyred’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pope Francis Retakes World Stage With a ‘Long-Awaited’ Visit to Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Cathol