 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdb3e701-492a-5ae1-855d-e36682b8ba97'}, {'abstract': 'The nominee, Vanita Gupta, had served as the department’s top civil rights official during the Obama administration. Some Republicans have already signaled that they will oppose her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/08/us/politics/vanita-gupta-justice-department.html', 'snippet': 'The nominee, Vanita Gupta, had served as the department’s top civil rights official during the Obama administration. Some Republicans have already signaled that they will oppose her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When the Obama administration convened a meeting in 2015 to discuss its investigation into police abuses in Ferguson, Mo., some officials were puzzled to see the conservative activist Grover Norquist in attendance, and even more surprised to learn that he was the guest of Vanita Gupta, a Justice Department official known for her work with progressive legal groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/08/us/politics/08dc-justice/merlin_182094858_4121b11a-f8b2-4200-9c9d-4bf822eba957-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/08/us/politics/08dc-justice/merlin_182094858_4121b11a-f8b2-4200-9c9d-4bf822eba957-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/08/us/politics/08dc-justice/merlin_182094858_4121b11a-f8b2-4200-9c9d-4bf822eba957-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/08/us/politics/08dc-justice/merlin_182094858_4121b11a-f8b2-4200-9c9d-4bf822eba957-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/08/us/politics/08dc-justice/merlin_182094858_4121b11a-f8b2-4200-9c9d-4bf822eba957-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/08/us/politics/08dc-justice/merlin_182094858_4121b11a-f8b2-4200-9c9d-4bf822eba957-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/08/us/politics/08dc-justice/merlin_182094858_4121b11a-f8b2-4200-9c9d-4bf822eba957-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden’s Pick for Justice Dept. No. 3 Wins Backing of Law Enforcement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biden’s Pick for a Top Justice Post Wins the Backing of Law Enforcement Groups', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Reform', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Assn of Chiefs of Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Judicial Crisis Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Vanita', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-09T01:06:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Benner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0858e60f-23e6-5ff5-bdf1-26710c77d166', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0858e60f-23e6-5ff5-bdf1-26710c77d166'}, {'abstract': 'Oishii Omakase strawberries are a flavorful, out-of-season berry grown in New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/08/dining/oiishi-omakase-strawberries.html', 'snippet': 'Oishii Omakase strawberries are a flavorful, out-of-season berry grown in New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late spring, local strawberries ripen and perfume the fields in some lucky areas. It’s that same alluring scent that wafts from a package of a Japanese breed of strawberries now growing year-round in a vertical indoor farm in New Jersey. Called Omakase strawberries, the Oishii brand berries make up for their lack of intense deep scarlet color with a penetrating aroma and a burst of juicy flavor that certainly outshines any others on the market now. They are prized by high-end restaurants; for tables at home they come at a jewel-like price, around $5 each, individually cradled in boxes of three ($15), six ($29) or eight ($50). Eli’s Manhattan, Eli’s Market in Grand Central Market and Olmsted in Brooklyn are among the places that sell them.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-berries/08burner-berries-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-berries/08burner-berries-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-berries/08burner-berries-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-berries/08burner-berries-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-berries/08burner-berries-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-berries/08burner-berries-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-berries/08burner-berries-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strawberries With a Heady Scent and Hefty Price Tag', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Savor: Juicy, Flavorful Aromatic and Pricey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strawberries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-09T01:14:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c023d075-8228-564b-8c5a-a5238b3822f2', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c023d075-8228-564b-8c5a-a5238b3822f2'}, {'abstract': 'Eat Offbeat has released its first cookbook, “The Kitchen Without Borders,” telling the stories of its chefs through their recipes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/08/dining/eat-offbeat-the-kitchen-without-borders.html', 'snippet': 'Eat Offbeat has released its first cookbook, “The Kitchen Without Borders,” telling the stories of its chefs through their recipes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New horizons open in “The Kitchen Without Borders,” a compilation of recipes from the immigrant and refugee chefs who worked with Eat Offbeat, a New York catering company. It was founded in 2015 by Manal and Wissam Kahi from Lebanon, and it pivoted to meal kit deliveries during the pandemic. The stories of 15 chefs fill the colorful pages of the cookbook, along with recipes from Syria, Afghanistan, Guinea, Sri Lanka, Nepal, Venezuela, Senegal and more. It’s home-cooking at its best, with eggplant dishes, salads and stews. There are inspirations, like a silken bell pepper soup from the Central African Republic, baklava richly interpreted as a cake by an Iranian chef, and Afghan chicken karahi, a quick simmer with spices and tomatoes. You may have to expand your pantry with items like berbere spices, barberries and piloncillo to prepare some of the recipes. Two percent of the price is being donated to the International Rescue Committee.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/10Burner-book/08Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/10Burner-book/08Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 753}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/10Burner-book/08Burner-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 817, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/10Burner-book/08Burner-book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1633, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/10Burner-book/08Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/10Burner-book/08Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/10Burner-book/08Burner-book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Celebration of Global Cuisines', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Cook: Recipes and Stories Celebrate Global Cuisines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-09T01:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc014e42-8010-5bde-a31b-a6ef91f3237f', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc014e42-8010-5bde-a31b-a6ef91f3237f'}, {'abstract': 'L.A. Burdick’s holiday collection riffs on Irish breakfast tea, whiskey and even stew, with some white chocolate sheep, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/08/dining/la-burdick-st-patricks-day-chocolate.html', 'snippet': 'L.A. Burdick’s holiday collection riffs on Irish breakfast tea, whiskey and even stew, with some white chocolate sheep, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chocolatier Michael Klug of L.A. Burdick, the chocolate company founded by Larry Burdick and based in Walpole, N.H., has dug deep to find inspiration in all things Irish for its new St. Patrick’s Day collection. Its box of bite-size bonbons contain fillings that evoke Irish coffee, Irish breakfast tea, Irish whiskey, and even carrots and thyme (to suggest Irish stew). The assortment also includes plump little white chocolate sheep, which replace L.A. Burdick’s signature chocolate mice with silken tails.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-chocolate/08burner-chocolate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-chocolate/08burner-chocolate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-chocolate/08burner-chocolate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-chocolate/08burner-chocolate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1637, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-chocolate/08burner-chocolate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-chocolate/08burner-chocolate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-chocolate/08burner-chocolate-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ode to Irish Classics, in Chocolate', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Give: Irish Classics, In Chocolate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "St Patrick's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-09T01:22:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/515f47e8-13bc-542f-97aa-2d2c10f07111', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/515f47e8-13bc-542f-97aa-2d2c10f07111'}, {'abstract': 'Haus’s latest aperitif is a spiced cherry that would be well suited to a manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/08/dining/haus-aperitif-spiced-cherry.html', 'snippet': 'Haus’s latest aperitif is a spiced cherry that would be well suited to a manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the newly popular aperitifs on the market are inspired by European-style amaros and vermouths, with strongly bitter or sweet flavors. But Haus, a wine-based collection from Sonoma County, Calif., sings its own tune, notably with Spiced Cherry, its newest flavor, neither bitter nor sweet, but fruity and tangy. It enlivens a manhattan or a cocktail like the aviation that calls for maraschino liqueur. Helena and Woody Hambrecht, who founded the company in 2019, start with unoaked chardonnay to which they add fresh herbs, botanicals, spices and fruit, minimal sweetening, and no artificial ingredients or colors. Haus aperitifs can be sipped on their own, chilled or on the rocks, mixed in a spritz or combined in cocktails. All are 18 to 20 percent alcohol, and there are six varieties. Haus is mostly sold online, $35 a bottle (750 milliliters) or $40 for four 200 milliliter (6.76 ounce) samplers.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-Drink/08Burner-Drink-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-Drink/08Burner-Drink-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-Drink/08Burner-Drink-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-Drink/08Burner-Drink-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1540, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-Drink/08Burner-Drink-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-Drink/08Burner-Drink-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-Drink/08Burner-Drink-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Aperitif With Cherry Flavor', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Give Your Manhattan An Infusion of Cherry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-09T01:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bae520d4-ae14-512e-af07-2a9c97756e4b', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bae520d4-ae14-512e-af07-2a9c97756e4b'}, {'abstract': 'Brisket and matzo-ball soup are the stars of the chef Michael Solomonov’s dinner, sold nationwide through Goldbelly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/08/dining/abe-fisher-passover-meal-kit.html', 'snippet': 'Brisket and matzo-ball soup are the stars of the chef Michael Solomonov’s dinner, sold nationwide through Goldbelly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matzo ball soup and brisket, the Passover perennials, anchor this new Seder dinner for delivery from Abe Fisher, a Jewish-style (non-kosher) restaurant in Philadelphia owned by the chef Michael Solomonov and Steve Cook. The soup is well-flavored, the epic matzo balls are floaters and the brisket, braised in coffee, is rich and tender. Starters include housemade “matzo,” seasoned with everything spice; beet tartare zapped with horseradish; and spreadable chicken rillettes. A carrot-walnut haroseth is included, but you’re on your own for the rest of the Seder plate. There’s no gefilte fish either, but a sweet potato and apple kugel and a fudgy chocolate dessert are in the package. Hot dishes reheat easily. It’s ample for four to six, and though it will not ship until March 24, it will keep until Passover.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-passover/08burner-passover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-passover/08burner-passover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-passover/08burner-passover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-passover/08burner-passover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-passover/08burner-passover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-passover/08burner-passover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08burner-passover/08burner-passover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Order Passover Dinner From Philly', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Celebrate: A Passover Dinner By Way of Philadelphia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Passover', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mail Order Companies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-09T01:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4490491-316e-58e5-a020-1d1cc300bf60', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4490491-316e-58e5-a020-1d1cc300bf60'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Binder Saini will hold hourlong chaat- and chai-making classes at his East Village restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/08/dining/veeray-da-dhaba-chaat-class.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Binder Saini will hold hourlong chaat- and chai-making classes at his East Village restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To add income during the pandemic, many chefs have taken to conducting virtual cooking classes. But now, with restaurant occupancy in New York City up to 35 percent, the chef Binder Saini will teach small groups in person in his East Village restaurant, Veeray da Dhaba. The subject, during Saturday and Sunday hourlong sessions every other week will be chaat, an almost infinitely variable street food snack, and chai. Different types of chaat will be taught throughout the series. To comply with safety protocols, Mr. Saini will conduct the class in the dining room. Participants will be seated at well-spaced tables, 35 percent capacity, with the ingredients for preparing the dish at each table.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-class/08Burner-class-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-class/08Burner-class-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-class/08Burner-class-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-class/08Burner-class-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-class/08Burner-class-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-class/08Burner-class-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/dining/08Burner-class/08Burner-class-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Learn to Make Chaat at Veeray da Dhaba', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Learn: Make Chaat and Chai At Veeray da Dhaba', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'},