': 'By Motoko Rich and Makiko Inoue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Makiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Inoue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d796f8-7fd7-521e-a60b-c775e0fca985', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d796f8-7fd7-521e-a60b-c775e0fca985'}, {'abstract': 'As the entertainment industry collapsed during the pandemic, several major health plans made it harder to qualify for insurance. Thousands lost it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/09/arts/coronavirus-actors.html', 'snippet': 'As the entertainment industry collapsed during the pandemic, several major health plans made it harder to qualify for insurance. Thousands lost it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ellyn Marie Marsh was getting ready to appear in a new off-Broadway musical last year when the pandemic struck, theaters were shut and her work evaporated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/00actors-heathcare-fairchild1/merlin_184548948_2d37cf0d-8628-4dd9-bf6c-6ecdf5ca4e36-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/00actors-heathcare-fairchild1/merlin_184548948_2d37cf0d-8628-4dd9-bf6c-6ecdf5ca4e36-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/05/arts/00actors-heathcare-fairchild1/merlin_184548948_2d37cf0d-8628-4dd9-bf6c-6ecdf5ca4e36-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r