: 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF MUSICIANS', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "ACTORS' FUND OF AMERICA", 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-09T20:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Stevens and Jeremy Fassler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fassler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c594961a-9d58-5889-994b-fdfb57c20189', 'word_count': 1640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c594961a-9d58-5889-994b-fdfb57c20189'}, {'abstract': 'Any nation that still has a monarchy in 2021 is proving itself to have a mortifying lack of revolutionary gumption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/09/opinion/meghan-harry-abolish-monarchy.html', 'snippet': 'Any nation that still has a monarchy in 2021 is proving itself to have a mortifying lack of revolutionary gumption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recent interview you may have heard about revealed that the British monarchy is a toxic den of backbiting and racism. And who would doubt it? There is nothing easier to believe than that an institution created to be the physical embodiment of classism is awash in inhumanity. Where the public response to this humdrum revelation has gone astray is in the widespread conviction that we should make the monarchy better. Not at all. You cannot turn a bottle of poison into a refreshing drink, no matter how much sugar you pour into it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/09/opinion/09Nolan1/merlin_156132372_54aed09c-6664-4ff9-a2b1-c85e13824896-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/09/opinion/09Nolan1/merlin_156132372_54aed09c-6664-4ff9-a2b1-c85e13824896-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/09/opinion/09Nolan1/merlin_156132372_54aed09c-6664-4ff9-a2b1-c85e13824896-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/09/opinion/09Nolan1/merlin_156132372_54aed09c-6664-4ff9-a2b1-c85e13824896-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1390, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/09/opinion/09Nolan1/09Nolan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/09/opinion/09Nolan1/09Nolan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/09/opinion/09Nolan1/09Nolan1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Down With the British Monarchy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], '