e 1950s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/09/books/review-transit-of-venus-shirley-hazzard.html', 'snippet': 'Shirley Hazzard’s “The Transit of Venus,” recently reissued, is a plushly written novel about two orphaned Australian sisters who arrive in England in the 1950s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a fact readily acknowledged that one can encounter some books simply too late in life to appreciate — or, in some cases, even tolerate — them. The famous examples include “The Catcher in the Rye,” most of the Beats, all of Anaïs Nin. But I’m more curious about the counterpoint: Those books said to require experience, and age, to unlock.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/books/review/09BOOKHAZZARD1/09BOOKHAZZARD1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 887, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/books/review/09BOOKHAZZARD1/09BOOKHAZZARD1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 887}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/books/review/09BOOKHAZZARD1/09BOOKHAZZARD1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 693, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/books/review/09BOOKHAZZARD1/09BOOKHAZZARD1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1385, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/books/review/09BOOKHAZZARD1/09BOOKHAZZARD1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/books/review/09BOOKHAZZARD1/09BOOKHAZZARD1-th