/europe/sarah-everard-women-protest.html', 'snippet': 'The “Reclaim These Streets” movement in Britain asks why the police demand sacrifices of women rather than forcing men to change to end violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps it was because pandemic lockdowns have left women clinging to whatever is left of their access to public space. Perhaps it was because after more than three years of the #MeToo movement, the police and society are still telling women to sacrifice their liberties to purchase a little temporary safety.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rage Over Sarah Everard Killing, ‘Women’s Bargain’ Is Put on Notice', 'kicker': 'The INTERPRETER', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In London, Fury Over the Lack of Safe Spaces for Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curfews', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Everard, Sarah', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-14T16:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Taub', 'person': [{'firs