cracked and slid from its perch, crashing through the portico of the parish’s administrative offices. Seconds later, the apse collapsed into a pile of rubble. At the far end of the nearly 40,000-square-foot complex, the gymnasium-like Santuario del Señor de Tula, a church built in 2001 to accommodate 1,000 parishioners, lurched a few centimeters to the west. The cavernous building pulled at the 19th-century arcade to which its northern facade had been anchored, shattering the delicate brick keystones.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '100', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/15/t-magazine/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/15/t-magazine/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/15/t-magazine/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/15/t-magazine/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1056, 'width': 1584, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/15/t-magazine/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIMQ-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/15/t-magazine/15tmag-jojutla-slide-JIM