 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/books/review/16Dorfman/16Dorfman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/16/books/review/16Dorfman/16Dorfman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/books/review/16Dorfman/16Dorfman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Nation’s Torturous Past Resembles ‘The Twilight Zone’', 'kicker': 'Fiction', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blaze of History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Twilight Zone (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Nona (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wimmer, Natasha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-16T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Dorfman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorfman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f24c3738-eaa2-5285-836e-6c98550f8f09', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f24c3738-eaa2-5285-836e-6c98550f8f09'}, {'abstract': 'From a Nevada “divorce ranch” to literary Dublin to 19th-century Sweden, these characters put relationships to the test.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/16/books/review/better-luck-next-time-julia-claiborne-johnson.html', 'snippet': 'From a Nevada “divorce ranch” to literary Dublin to 19th-century Sweden, these characters put relationships to the test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s easy to see why Julia Claiborne Johnson filled BETTER LUCK NEXT TIME (Custom House, 288 pp., $28.99) with movie-star look-alikes. Doesn’t a romantic comedy set on a 1930s Nevada dude ranch teeming with about-to-be-divorced women owe a certain debt to the era’s big-screen classics? Then again, it’s hard to believe a cinematic version could be any more fun than the small-page antics of the aptly named Flying Leap’s two hired hands and the pair of wealthy “guests” who seem determined to make their required stint as legal state residents as memorable as possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/books/review/Becker_HistFict1/Becker_HistFict1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 429, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/books/review/Becker_HistFict1/Becker_HistFict1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 429, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/books/review/Becker_HistFict1/Becker_HistFict1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/02/26/books/review/Becker_HistFict1/Becker_HistFict1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/26/books/review/Becker_HistFict1/Becker_HistFict1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Historical Novels Explore the Strength of Human Connection', 'kicker': 'Fiction', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Past Caring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Better Luck Next Time: A Novel (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Julia Claiborne (Author)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nora: A Love Story of Nora and James Joyce (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, Nuala", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'To Cook a Bear: A Novel (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niemi, Mikael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-16T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alida Becker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Becker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/214757a9-aa40-5392-a0fb-c874dd6d8ed6', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/214757a9-aa40-5392-a0fb-c874dd6d8ed6'}, {'abstract': 'After our mom died, I turned to her beloved pastime for comfort. It opened up a new way to communicate with my family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/16/magazine/chinese-tv-dramas-story-of-yanxi-palace.html', 'snippet': 'After our mom died, I turned to her beloved pastime for comfort. It opened up a new way to communicate with my family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I tell people my sister is 14 months older than me, some marvel at how close we must be. Others joke that my parents got busy fast. The joke is true, but my sister and I have never been close. We couldn’t be more different. I’m louder, taller and blunter. She’s quieter, shorter and sweeter. When we were young, I barreled through Michigan forests on my bike while she buried her head in Nancy Drew books. Because my sister was more obedient and a better student than I was, I perceived that she was the favored child. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-lor/21mag-lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-lor/21mag-lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-lor/21mag-lor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-lor/21mag-lor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-lor/21mag-lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-lor/21mag-lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-lor/21mag-lor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Chinese Dramas Helped Me Build a Relationship With My Sister', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommen