ions', 'value': 'TikTok (ByteDance)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-16T18:57:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Callie Holtermann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Callie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holtermann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50a21250-31c5-5ead-b1b9-29a09f5a5d53', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50a21250-31c5-5ead-b1b9-29a09f5a5d53'}, {'abstract': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/16/style/tiny-modern-love-stories-mami-sent-me-to-check-you-out.html', 'snippet': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a dutiful girlfriend, I accompanied Arturo to J.F.K. Airport to pick up his sister, who was arriving from Buenos Aires. Greeting her, I casually asked what brought her to New York. “Mami sent me to check you out,” she said. Years later, Mami was visiting us. She offered to buy me a replacement diamond for the one that fell out of my engagement ring. “Oh, I can’t allow you to buy me something so expensive,” I said. Her reply? “Please do, because you are everything I hoped for in a wife for my son.” How could I refuse? — Phyllis Meyers', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/23/fashion/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/02/23/fashion/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/23/fashion/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/23/fashion/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/23/fashion/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/02/23/fashion/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/23/fashion/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4/00MARCH-TINYLOVEILLO4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Love Stories: ‘Mami Sent Me to Check You Out’', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-16T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1371c9d2-d480-5f9a-a303-adc16115a482', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1371c9d2-d480-5f9a-a303-adc16115a482'}, {'abstract': 'In this new short film, an artist finds hope in an unlikely place — the city’s storefront gates, rolling up day after day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/16/opinion/hallelujah-anyway-anyway-covid-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'In this new short film, an artist finds hope in an unlikely place — the city’s storefront gates, rolling up day after day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For almost three decades, I’ve been making visual art with New York City at its center. I’m especially drawn to everyday moments that, when you focus on them, have unexpected emotional power: the riveted expressions of lunchgoers scanning a salad bar, the split-second disorientation of commuters emerging from the subway onto the street. I work mostly in public, but I don’t know how to do that right now. So I find myself looking back on footage I shot in the past to try to make sense of the present. In the short documentary above, I revisited a video I shot in the early 1990s, of shopkeepers near my East Village apartment throwing open their gates in the morning, to reflect on the perpetual change and resilience that mark life in New York City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Lived Through the AIDS Crisis and Now Covid. N.Y.C. Got Me Through.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-16T19:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/727723ff-9cca-53c3-a9b0-5f794d156f2e', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/727723ff-9cca-53c3-a9b0-5f794d156f2e'}, {'abstract': 'I have spent years poring over archives to illuminate the lives of those bought and sold by a prominent order of Jesuit priests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/16/us/catholic-church-enslavement.html', 'snippet': 'I have spent years poring over archives to illuminate the lives of those bought and sold by a prominent order of Jesuit priests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1717, a prominent Jesuit priest handed over a sprawling Maryland plantation controlled by his Catholic order to a new owner. Amid the hogs and milk cows, candlesticks and chalices were 15 enslaved men, women and children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/16rr-enslaved1/16rr-enslaved1-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/10/us/16rr-enslaved1/16rr-enslaved1-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 574}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/16rr-enslaved1/16rr-enslaved1-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 980, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/16rr-enslaved1/16rr-enslaved1-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1664, 'width': 1739, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/16rr-enslaved1/16rr-enslaved1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/10/us/16rr-enslaved1/16rr-enslaved1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/16rr-enslaved1/16rr-enslaved1-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Research Into the History of Catholic Slaveholding Transformed My Understanding of My Church.', 'kicker': 'Race/Related', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery (Historical)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Descendants of Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jesuit Conference of Canada and the United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-16T19:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel L. Swarns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Swarns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea2ab5b7-1925-5ecc-9d9f-0227fd9547f3', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea2ab5b7-1925-5ecc-9d9f-0227fd9547f3'}, {'abstract': 'Keep the ban of the former president in place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/16/opinion/facebook-trump-ban.html', 'snippet': 'Keep the ban of the former president in place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are a public official, there’s no more effective or efficient place to lie than on Facebook. It’s company policy — meaning the policy of the chief executive, Mark Zuckerberg — to roll out the red carpet to all manner of political falsehood and obfuscation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/opinion/16bensinger-illo/16bensinger-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/16/opinion/16bensinger-illo/16bensinger-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/opinion/16bensinger-illo/16bensinger-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/opinion/16bensinger-illo/16bensinger-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/opinion/16bensinger-illo/16bensinger-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/16/opinion/16bensinger-illo/16bensinger-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ran