ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/180fe134-1a53-5313-b968-d23e41e3baef', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/180fe134-1a53-5313-b968-d23e41e3baef'}, {'abstract': 'With climate concerns growing, steel companies face an inevitable crunch. ArcelorMittal sees solutions, but the costs are likely to run into tens of billions of dollars in Europe alone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/17/business/steel-emissions-arcelor-mittal.html', 'snippet': 'With climate concerns growing, steel companies face an inevitable crunch. ArcelorMittal sees solutions, but the costs are likely to run into tens of billions of dollars in Europe alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few materials are more essential than steel, yet steel mills are among the leading polluters. They burn coke, a derivative of coal, and belch millions of tons of greenhouse gases. Roughly two tons of carbon dioxide rises into the atmosphere for every ton of steel made using blast furnaces.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/business/17mittal-1/merlin_184794102_8b5920c5-4935-41a5-be04-f537c274dfa6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/17/business/17mittal-1/merlin_184794102_8b5920c5-4935-41a5-be04-f537c274dfa6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/business/17mittal-1/merlin_184794102_8b5920c5-4935-41a5-be04-f537c274dfa6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/business/17mittal-1/merlin_18479