'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5261b3-0c37-5d14-ba0b-7e85222bfab3', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5261b3-0c37-5d14-ba0b-7e85222bfab3'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s admissions essays became a platform for high school seniors to reflect on the pandemic, race and loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/17/us/covid-college-admissions.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s admissions essays became a platform for high school seniors to reflect on the pandemic, race and loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year perhaps more than ever before, the college essay has served as a canvas for high school seniors to reflect on a turbulent and, for many, sorrowful year. It has been a psychiatrist’s couch, a road map to a more hopeful future, a chance to pour out intimate feelings about loneliness and injustice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/us/00virus-college-essays2/merlin_182275944_ce6761c6-dd5c-4b50-88a9-01b169f4e79e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/10/us/00virus-college-essays2/merlin_182275944_ce6761c6-dd5c-4b50-88a9-01b169f4e79e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/us/00virus-college-essays2/merlin_182275944_ce6761c6-dd5c-4b50-88a9-01b169f4e79e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/us/00virus-college-essays2/merlin_182275944_ce6761c6-dd5c-4b50-88a9-01b169f4e79e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/us/00virus-college-essays2/merlin_182275944_ce6761c6-dd5c-4b50-88a9-01b169f4e79e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/10/us/00virus-college-essays2/merlin_182275944_ce6761c6-dd5c-4b50-88a9-01b169f4e79e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/10/us/00virus-college-essays2/merlin_182275944_ce6761c6-dd5c-4b50-88a9-01b169f4e79e-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘When Normal Life Stopped’: College Essays Reflect a Turbulent Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'College Essays in a Year  Of Grief and Turmoil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-17T09:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76530553-c78b-53f4-8608-07ff3951960f', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76530553-c78b-53f4-8608-07ff3951960f'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “This Is the Fire: What I Say to My Friends About Racism,” by Don Lemon', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/17/books/review/this-is-the-fire-what-i-say-to-my-friends-about-racism-by-don-lemon-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “This Is the Fire: What I Say to My Friends About Racism,” by Don Lemon', 'lead_paragraph': 'A comfortable two-hour drive from the Midtown headquarters of CNN, not far from the Sag Harbor home I share with my fiancé, Tim, a truncated boardwalk path cuts through the dune grass and gives way to tawny sand on the beach at Sag Harbor Bay. A stone marker at the trailhead honors the founder of this extraordinary enclave, an African American neighborhood on prime beachfront real estate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘This Is the Fire: What I Say to My Friends About Racism,’ by Don Lemon: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lemon, Don', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'This Is the Fire: What I Say to My Friends About Racism (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-17T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/36129cc8-8f97-5054-9e28-b3d81c67a5e1', 'word_count': 3054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36129cc8-8f97-5054-9e28-b3d81c67a5e1'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats and Republicans increasingly live apart, all the way down to the neighborhood level.', 'web_url': 'https://