n', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Michigan University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Carolina State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Central Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Connecticut', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of South Carolina', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-18T04:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Weiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/728cbcd5-d2aa-5e58-b534-f3d13e6cee39', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/728cbcd5-d2aa-5e58-b534-f3d13e6cee39'}, {'abstract': 'In an era of shuttered stadiums, a solitary Real Sociedad fan sends scoring updates to his city with flares, preserving a tradition linking the soccer team with another era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/18/sports/soccer/real-sociedad-flares-cohetero.html', 'snippet': 'In an era of shuttered stadiums, a solitary Real Sociedad fan sends scoring updates to his city with flares, preserving a tradition linking the soccer team with another era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As soon as the ball crosses the line, Juan Iturralde is on his feet. He darts back inside his suite, heading for the door. He pauses only briefly, to snatch two bottle rockets from a plastic bag placed carefully, deliberately, in his path. Its location is strategic: Iturralde is, essentially, in the news business, and every second counts.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'m