nt_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Courtney Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Courtney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ed83ee1-860b-505d-a2bd-67f8994e8742', 'word_count': 1393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ed83ee1-860b-505d-a2bd-67f8994e8742'}, {'abstract': 'A reminder that there is always a chance at being nurtured by the thing that brings you pain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/18/magazine/poem-the-year-of-the-goldfinches.html', 'snippet': 'A reminder that there is always a chance at being nurtured by the thing that brings you pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have seen a goldfinch only once or twice in my life, and I learned the word only when I had a bird-feeder and therefore reason to notice. Ada Limón is a straight genius when it comes to noticing. Her poems turn the way horses seem to birth full-grown horses into a metaphor for love, and turn goldfinches into a reminder that there is always a chance at being nurtured by the thing that brings you pain — or at least a possibility that it won’t bury you. Selected by Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-poem/21mag-poem-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 232, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-poem/21mag-poem-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 232}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-poem/21mag-poem-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-poem/21mag-poem-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-poem/21mag-poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-poem/21mag-poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/magazine/21mag-poem/21mag-poem-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem : The Year of the Goldfinches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limon, Ada (1976- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-18T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ada Limón and Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Limón', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Reginald', 'middlename': 'Dwayne', 'lastname': 'Betts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/338fa3c6-04a2-5d9b-8a07-1ba778a1cab6', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/338fa3c6-04a2-5d9b-8a07-1ba778a1cab6'}, {'abstract': 'They went undercover, smuggled revolvers in teddy bears and were bearers of the truth. Why hadn’t I heard their stories?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/18/opinion/sunday/Jewish-women-Nazi-fighters.html', 'snippet': 'They went undercover, smuggled revolvers in teddy bears and were bearers of the truth. Why hadn’t I heard their stories?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1943, Niuta Teitelbaum strolled into a Gestapo apartment on Chmielna Street in central Warsaw and faced three Nazis. A 24-year-old Jewish woman who had studied history at Warsaw University, Niuta was likely now dressed in her characteristic guise as a Polish farm girl with a kerchief tied around her braided blond hair.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18batalion/18batalion-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 883, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18batalion/18batalion-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 883}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18batalion/18batalion-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 696, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18batalion/18batalion-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1392, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18batalion/18batalion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18batalion/18batalion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18batalion/18batalion-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Nazi-Fighting Women of the Jewish Resistance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Women of the Jewish Resistance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warsaw (Poland)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-18T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Batalion', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Batalion', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/41d519ab-23ce-5956-98b0-224b4adb60c6', 'word_count': 2368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41d519ab-23ce-5956-98b0-224b4adb60c6'}, {'abstract': 'But it’s not the same as Facebook’s. C.E.O. Brian Chesky discusses why he and Mark Zuckerberg have different consequences to consider.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/18/opinion/sway-kara-swisher-brian-chesky.html', 'snippet': 'But it’s not the same as Facebook’s. C.E.O. Brian Chesky discusses why he and Mark Zuckerberg have different consequences to consider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next week, tech executives Mark Zuckerberg, Jack Dorsey and Sundar Pichai will be questioned about the ways misinformation on their sites may have contributed to the Capitol attack. But theirs aren’t the only platforms used by the Jan. 6 mob. A number of those charged in the Capitol riot used Airbnb to book their stays in the Washington area. Now, a team at Airbnb is working with law enforcement to track warrants and arrests connected to the attacks. The company is actively de-platforming individuals who have been arrested or who have warrants out for their arrest. Going forward, this team will also be monitoring political congregations, large gatherings and events like the Fourth of July for potential dangerous activity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18sway-chesky-image/18sway-chesky-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18sway-chesky-image/18sway-chesky-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18sway-chesky-image/18sway-chesky-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18sway-chesky-image/18sway-chesky-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1619, 'width': 1619, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18sway-chesky-image/18sway-chesky-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/18/opinion/18sway-chesky-image/18sway-chesky-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7