'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f40073-c906-54cf-9b93-e08957645f19', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f40073-c906-54cf-9b93-e08957645f19'}, {'abstract': 'An experiment by Japanese researchers revealed how just a few distracted walkers really can throw off the movements of a whole crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/18/science/distracted-walking-phone.html', 'snippet': 'An experiment by Japanese researchers revealed how just a few distracted walkers really can throw off the movements of a whole crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a crosswalk at rush hour, you thread your way through the oncoming crowd, your eyes passing over the faces before you. This wayfinding might feel like something you’re doing on your own. But scientists who study the movements of crowds have found that a simple trip through a crowd is much more like a dance we perform with those around us.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/science/17TB-CROSSWALK/17TB-CROSSWALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/17/science/17TB-CROSSWALK/17TB-CROSSWALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/science/17TB-CROSSWALK/17TB-CROSSWALK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/17/science/17TB-CROSSWALK/17TB-CROSSWALK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 