: 'Albeck-Ripka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06871791-8599-5b62-83e7-24cfb5bb4f61', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06871791-8599-5b62-83e7-24cfb5bb4f61'}, {'abstract': 'Marie-Louise Sciò bounces among her family’s three hotels — including the legendary Il Pellicano in Tuscany — but her own flat is a different sort of retreat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/18/t-magazine/marie-louise-scio-design-rome.html', 'snippet': 'Marie-Louise Sciò bounces among her family’s three hotels — including the legendary Il Pellicano in Tuscany — but her own flat is a different sort of retreat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIKE THE WILD Tuscan orchids that burst forth in shades of lemon and violet along the craggy coast of Italy’s Argentario promontory, Marie-Louise Sciò’s life comes into full bloom in spring. It’s then that she prepares for the busy summer season at her family’s three hotels, the Mezzatorre on the island of Ischia, La Posta Vecchia in Ladispoli and Il Pellicano, the legendary resort cradled in the volcanic rocks above the seaside town of Porto Ercole. Since 2011, Sciò has been not only the embodiment of these properties’ glamorously Italian spirit but their creative director and C.E.O. Her father, Robert Sciò, bought Hotel Il Pellicano in 1979 from Patricia Graham, an American heiress, and her British husband, Michael, an ex-R.A.F. fighter pilot, who had built it in the mid-60s as a private villa and club. Its languid, sun-bleached charm was immortalized by the photographer Slim Aarons. These days, it is the 44-year-old Sciò who oversees its 47 rooms and two terrace restaurants. With an offhand manner that belies a great deal of preparation, she seamlessly coordinates each aspect of Il Pellicano. “It’s all-consuming,” she says, “but in an amazing way.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '43', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/t-magazine/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/18/t-magazine/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/t-magazine/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/t-magazine/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 1252, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/t-magazine/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/18/t-magazine/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/t-magazine/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy/18tmag-scio-slide-9B5P-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rome Apartment a Hotelier Calls Home', 'kicker': 'by design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roman Holiday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subje