4e-b846-8a80d3a6882c'}, {'abstract': 'In their agreements with the league, networks promoted their digital rights. But the structure of the deals allows consumers to watch most games without subscribing to a streaming service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/19/sports/nfl-media-rights-deal-espn-amazon-fox-nbc-cbs.html', 'snippet': 'In their agreements with the league, networks promoted their digital rights. But the structure of the deals allows consumers to watch most games without subscribing to a streaming service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The biggest conglomerates in television collectively agreed to spend more than $100 billion to continue putting N.F.L. games on their broadcast and cable television channels for the next decade, but the way they announced the deals on Thursday did not make that immediately apparent.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/19/sports/19nfl-media-web-1/merlin_184838319_c437a775-557c-4d85-8187-2eb1e43a4138-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/19/sports/19nfl-media-web-1/merlin_184838319_c437a775-557c-4d85-8187-2eb1e43a4138-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/19/sports/19nfl-media-web-1/merlin_184838319_c437a775-557c-4d85-8187-2eb1e43a4138-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/19/sports/19nfl-media-web-1/merlin_184838319_c437a775-557c-4d85-8187-2eb1e43a4138-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank'