ald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinken, Antony J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-19T10:28:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/56589022-ea5c-5a4d-a490-6b146426e75a', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56589022-ea5c-5a4d-a490-6b146426e75a'}, {'abstract': 'Britain’s “one-jab” strategy is working, offering lessons for the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/19/briefing/atlanta-shootings-ncaa-mens-division-teen-vogue.html', 'snippet': 'Britain’s “one-jab” strategy is working, offering lessons for the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The global leaders in Covid-19 vaccination rates are Israel and the United Arab Emirates. After them come a handful of countries that have each given between 30 and 45 shots for every 100 residents, including the United States, Britain, Bahrain, Chile and Serbia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/19/lens/19ambriefing-promo/19ambriefing-britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/19/lens/19ambriefing-promo/19ambriefing-britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/19/lens/19ambriefing-promo/19ambriefing-britain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 