2ca-5015-bf36-bff5e70d77ee', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audiocontainer/3e631625-f2ca-5015-bf36-bff5e70d77ee'}, {'abstract': 'Make the Persian chicken stew known as khoresh-e fesenjoon, coconut macaroons with chocolate, or a cheesy baked polenta with tomato sauce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/19/dining/what-to-cook-this-weekend.html', 'snippet': 'Make the Persian chicken stew known as khoresh-e fesenjoon, coconut macaroons with chocolate, or a cheesy baked polenta with tomato sauce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Nowruz, the Persian New Year, is tomorrow, and, if the feasting and exchanging of presents will be muted this year because of the pandemic, we’ve still got loads of recipes appropriate to the holiday. Take a look at Samin Nosrat’s khoresh-e fesenjoon, for instance, a Persian chicken stew with pomegranate molasses and walnuts (above). You could serve that with salad-e shirazi, a salad of cucumber, tomatoes and onion. That would be a very nice meal. (And it would yield tremendous leftovers, too.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/14Iranianrex7/merlin_154113903_ae20974a-5c45-4c79-b7c3-0ef8a615fc47-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/14Iranianrex7/merlin_154113903_ae20974a-5c45-4c79-b7c3-0ef8a615fc47-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/14Iranianrex7/merlin_154113903_ae20974a-5c45-4c79-b7c3-0ef8a615fc47-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/14Iranianrex7/merlin_154113903_ae20974a-5c45-4c