 right. She’s part of a new wave of lawmakers more interested in brand-building than lawmaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When Representative Marjorie Taylor Greene was expelled from her congressional committees as punishment for conspiracy mongering and violent statements, she embraced her exile, declaring that she had been “freed” from the obligation to participate in the drudgery of legislating.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/09/us/politics/00dc-cong-influencers1/merlin_183275793_cbf9313e-bbe3-4b98-a29e-96a8a4d7a547-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/02/09/us/politics/00dc-cong-influencers1/merlin_183275793_cbf9313e-bbe3-4b98-a29e-96a8a4d7a547-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/09/us/politics/00dc-cong-influencers1/merlin_183275793_cbf9313e-bbe3-4b98-a29e-96a8a4d7a547-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/09/us/politics/00dc-cong-influencers1/merlin_183275793_cbf9313e-bbe3-4b98-a29e-96a8a4d7a547-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/09/us/politics/00dc-cong-influencers1/00dc-cong-influencers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/02/09/us/politics/00dc-cong-influencers1/00dc-cong-influencers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbn