ter-newsletter-healing-in-the-form-of-a-designer-dress.html', 'snippet': 'And: A basketball legend’s daughter says “I do”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The emotional upheaval of a serious illness can make it difficult to cope in all aspects of life. When Emilie Poplett, the writer of this week’s Modern Love essay, developed frightening symptoms — fever, weight loss, bruising — she turned to medical professionals and even unorthodox healers for an explanation. While enduring numerous tests and painful procedures, each one inconclusive, Ms. Poplett found solace and temporary healing by buying pre-owned luxury garments. Each purchase was a hopeful promise of a future where she would be well enough to wear them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/25/fashion/loveletter/loveletter-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/25/fashion/loveletter/loveletter-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/25/fashion/loveletter/loveletter-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1018, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/25/fashion/loveletter/loveletter-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1057, 'width': 1050, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/25/fashion/loveletter/loveletter-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/25/fashion/loveletter/loveletter-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/25/fashion/loveletter/loveletter-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love Letter: Healing in the Form of a Designer Dress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barkley, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-20T13:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charanna Alexander', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alexander', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e04f1c7-17c9-5b7e-83e0-6abd0465c0b6', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e04f1c7-17c9-5b7e-83e0-6abd0465c0b6'}, {'abstract': 'There are no easy options when it comes to collecting back rent these days, so landlords would be wise to seek compromises with tenants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/20/realestate/landlords-covid-eviction-rent.html', 'snippet': 'There are no easy options when it comes to collecting back rent these days, so landlords would be wise to seek compromises with tenants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q: My sister owns a single-family home in Queens Village with a tenant who stopped paying rent well over a year ago and refuses to move. At this point, my sister wants to sell the house — she can’t afford to keep paying the mortgage while a family lives there rent-free. But can she sell a house that’s occupied by a tenant who won’t pay? And for how much?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/realestate/20Ask/20Ask-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/21/realestate/20Ask/20Ask-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 118}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/realestate/20Ask/20Ask-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 201, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/realestate/20Ask/20Ask-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/realestate/20Ask/20Ask-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/21/realestate/20Ask/20Ask-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/realestate/20Ask/20Ask-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Tenant Won’t Pay, but Won’t Go. What Can I Do?', 'kicker': 'Ask Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Can My Sister Sell Her House With a Nonpaying Tenant Still There?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security Act (202