': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/31c26b38-19c0-5d1f-821e-379d40f014a5', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31c26b38-19c0-5d1f-821e-379d40f014a5'}, {'abstract': 'Like every other industry, the art world is in a digital pivot right now. And people are logging on to creatively browse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/20/at-home/online-art-fairs.html', 'snippet': 'Like every other industry, the art world is in a digital pivot right now. And people are logging on to creatively browse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you’re accustomed to building  your social calendar around must-see art fairs or are still confused why an event named after the Swiss city of Basel sets Miami alight each year, the past year saw a seismic shift for the art world’s aficionados and casual observers alike. With the rise of the online art fair, suddenly everyone had an opportunity to see some of the world’s most exciting art without leaving the couch.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/multimedia/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/21/multimedia/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/multimedia/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/21/multimedia/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR/21ah-ONLINEARTCOLOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_na