me': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-22T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Goldsmith and Samuel Moyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldsmith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/427a8af4-1255-5576-b3fe-3f1c40b05302', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/427a8af4-1255-5576-b3fe-3f1c40b05302'}, {'abstract': 'Countries should know that a successful rollout is not just about delivery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/22/opinion/astrazeneca-vaccine-trust.html', 'snippet': 'Countries should know that a successful rollout is not just about delivery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Medicines Agency, Europe’s top drug regulator, confirmed last Thursday that the Oxford-AstraZeneca Covid-19 vaccine is safe. And on Monday, results from a large clinical trial in the U.S. found that the vaccine is 79 percent effective with no serious side effects. In some ways, this shouldn’t be news: It had previously received approval by the E.M.A. and some 20 million people in Europe have already received doses, largely without issues. But earlier in the week, several European countries temporarily halted inoculations out of concern that it caused blood clots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/opinion/22Larson/merlin_185344203_86b52092-3cd3-4fa1-b800-e44a6331e7e1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/22/opinion/22Larson/merlin_185344203_86b52092-3cd3-4fa1-b800-e44a6331e7e1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/opinion/22Larson/merlin_185344203_86b52092-3cd3-4fa1-b800-e44a6331e7e1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/opinion/22Larson/merlin_185344203_86b52092-3cd3-4fa1-b800-e44a6331e7e1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/opinion/22Larson/merlin_185344203_86b52092-3cd3-4fa1-b800-e44a6331e7e1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/22/opinion/22Larson/merlin_185344203_86b52092-3cd3-4fa1-b800-e44a6331e7e1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/opinion/22Larson/merlin_185344203_86b52092-3cd3-4fa1-b800-e44a6331e7e1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Want to Restore Trust in the AstraZeneca Vaccine? Start Here.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blood Clots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AstraZeneca PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Medicines Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-22T09:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heidi J. Larson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heidi', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Larson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/898323a5-e148-5441-a365-da6fda5476df', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/898323a5-e148-5441-a365-da6fda5476df'}, {'abstract': 'Parosmia, a condition that causes phantom odors and a lingering symptom of Covid-19 for some people, has been affecting relationships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/22/style/smell-covid-dating-parosmia.html', 'snippet': 'Parosmia, a condition that causes phantom odors and a lingering symptom of Covid-19 for some people, has been affecting relationships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samantha LaLiberte, a social worker in Nashville, thought she had made a full recovery from Covid-19. But in mid-November, about seven months after she’d been sick, a takeout order smelled so foul that she threw it away. When she stopped by the house of a friend who was cooking, she ran outside and vomited on the front lawn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/fashion/18PAROSMIA1/merlin_