on yet another Ozymandias. Still, tucked amid these dunes are a handful of modest architectural triumphs, built during a brief gust of Modernism that swept through the area in the mid-20th century. One of them, known as the Sugarman House, a hyperminimalist 1963 concrete shrine of jutting rectangles\u2009—\u2009part sand castle, part bachelor’s lair\u2009—\u2009serves as a case study of the work of the underrecognized American designer Ward Bennett.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '83', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/t-magazine/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/22/t-magazine/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/t-magazine/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/t-magazine/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1073, 'width': 1611, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/t-magazine/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/22/t-magazine/22tmag-wardbennett-slide-HGYK-copy/22t