'persons', 'value': 'Obiaya, Ikechukwu', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-22T17:43:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adenike Olanrewaju', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adenike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olanrewaju', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f242cdda-c6ac-523e-bb32-903dde55f9b4', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f242cdda-c6ac-523e-bb32-903dde55f9b4'}, {'abstract': 'It’s just a few weeks before the 2016 election, and lots of Republicans are feeling like they don’t recognize their own party. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/22/will-i-know-anyone-at-this-party.html', 'snippet': 'It’s just a few weeks before the 2016 election, and lots of Republicans are feeling like they don’t recognize their own party. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s just a few weeks before the 2016 election, and lots of Republicans are feeling like they don’t recognize their own party. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will I Know Anyone at This Party?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-03-22T18:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'audiocontainer', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': '', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://audiocontainer/7df4aea9-8e2b-5dd3-b827-836f035a23f3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audiocontainer/7df4aea9-8e2b-5dd3-b827-836f035a23f3'}, {'abstract': 'The woodworker Sophie Sellu brings the same patience and care with which she makes her wares to this cherished recipe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/22/t-magazine/sophie-sellu-tagine-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'The woodworker Sophie Sellu brings the same patience and care with which she makes her wares to this cherished recipe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even today, when most household items are readily available, certain products cannot be rushed — and a subset of old-school artisans continue to take their stubborn time. Consider, for example, the 32-year-old woodworker Sophie Sellu. As the founder and lone employee of the London brand Grain and Knot, she spends six to eight consecutive weeks cutting, carving and sanding a series of brushes, vases, spatulas, cutting boards and other pieces until she’s amassed at least 50. Then she photographs them herself, posts them online and announces their availability — at which point they sell out within an hour. (The next drop will be on April 14.) “Because people can’t have Grain and Knot all the time,” she says, “it makes them want it even more.” Once the orders are in, she wraps the parcels, lugs them to the post office and begins the process anew, cycling through another period of tension and release.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy/16tmag-sellu-slide-WGW8-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048