e', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d898e86-c40a-57ff-9830-814243862be5', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d898e86-c40a-57ff-9830-814243862be5'}, {'abstract': 'The AAPI Love Taste Bud shirt brings attention to Asian-American and Pacific Islander-owned restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/22/dining/aapi-community-fund.html', 'snippet': 'The AAPI Love Taste Bud shirt brings attention to Asian-American and Pacific Islander-owned restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The graphic designer Eileen Tjan and the social media director Michael Chan have designed a T-shirt that brings attention to Asian-American and Pacific Islander-owned restaurants, while raising money for the Support the AAPI Community Fund. “There are many trendy, high-end fashion T-shirt designs out there, but we wanted to make one that had purpose,” Mr. Chan said. The back of the shirt lists restaurants in 25 states, along with a handful of food companies. (More than two dozen New York restaurants are included.) The long-sleeve shirts are available to preorder through March 28 and will be shipped starting April 12.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/24/dining/22burner-shirt/22burner-shirt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/24/dining/22burner-shirt/22burner-shirt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/24/dining/22burner-shirt/22burner-shirt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'lega