21.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Sunday about an alliance of lawyers, lobbyists and Orthodox Jewish leaders that influenced clemency grants by President Donald J. Trump misstated the recommendation made by Rabbi Sholom D. Lipskar at the 2014 sentencing of Eliyahu Weinstein. Rabbi Lipskar sought a punishment of five years in prison plus five years of house arrest, not five years of house arrest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: March 23, 2021', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-03-23T01:49:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/f63126f3-149f-5dcb-8802-4cf24083095b', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f63126f3-149f-5dcb-8802-4cf24083095b'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Schoenholz captivates us with his Tuesday puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/22/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2021-03-23.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Schoenholz captivates us with his Tuesday puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY PUZZLE — One of the things I love about crossword puzzles is the wide variety of trivia and knowledge they contain. Even in an early-week puzzle like this, I’ll probably end up not knowing a few answers. Asking a friend, using the reveal tool or taking to the internet to find the answers to a crossword are all not only allowed, but I would also even go as far as to encourage it. There’s no fun in being stuck.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/23/crosswords/23wordplay-extracharge-ta/23wordplay-extracharge-ta-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarg