/22ALLGASNOBRAKES-03-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He Had an R.V., a Camera and a Plan to Document America. Was That Enough?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘All Gas No Brakes’ May Have Hit Empty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'All Gas No Brakes (Web-Original Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callaghan, Andrew (Journalist)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-23T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Taylor Lorenz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lorenz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d989ed7d-9b5c-5cef-a94a-172330a28c60', 'word_count': 1668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d989ed7d-9b5c-5cef-a94a-172330a28c60'}, {'abstract': 'The Fed chair, Jerome Powell, has become a popular Main Street champion. Here’s a history of the advocacy that made this possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/23/opinion/powell-federal-reserve-inflation.html', 'snippet': 'The Fed chair, Jerome Powell, has become a popular Main Street champion. Here’s a history of the advocacy that made this possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2015, I was working as an economist at the Federal Reserve. If someone told you then that in 2020 a deadly pandemic would shut down life as we knew it and that in the midst of a stop-and-go response from Congress, a Federal Reserve ch