are houses you don’t want, that, nevertheless, enter your life and bring with them other lives, whole other worlds. There are countries you visit that lay hold of you and don’t let go, even if you diligently attempt to remain a tourist. These thoughts have been incubating in the mind of Shay Senna ever since she—a Black American woman with scant interest in the continent of Africa except as a near-mythical motherland—unexpectedly and unwillingly became mistress of the Red House, a sprawling household in northwestern Madagascar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Red Island House,’ by Andrea Lee: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-03-23T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dad7aee7-0b78-58c4-9a9d-9671787b6d34', 'word_count': 2808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dad7aee7-0b78-58c4-9a9d-9671787b6d34'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Moonshadow was at the checkout at King Soopers with her son, buying food while waiting for her laundry to be done nearby, when she heard shots being fired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/23/us/the-shots-are-getting-closer-witnesses-recounted-moments-of-terror-inside-and-outside-the-store.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Moonshadow was at the checkout at King Soopers with her son, buying food while waiting for her laundry to be done nearby, when she heard shots being fired.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/22/us/22colorado-shooting/22colorado-shooting-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'lega