sal, neither Netanyahu nor opposition has clear path to a majority.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-03-23T20:42:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Kingsley and Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kingsley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9332639-ad23-5782-8336-4466275e8c89', 'word_count': 1499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9332639-ad23-5782-8336-4466275e8c89'}, {'abstract': 'As Republican legislatures seek to usher in a raft of new voting restrictions, they are being prodded by an array of party leaders and outside groups working to coordinate the efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/23/us/politics/republican-voter-laws.html', 'snippet': 'As Republican legislatures seek to usher in a raft of new voting restrictions, they are being prodded by an array of party leaders and outside groups working to coordinate the efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late January, a small group of dedicated volunteers from the conservative Heritage Action for America met with Republican legislators in Georgia, delivering a letter containing detailed proposals for rolling back access to voting. Within days, bills to restrict voting access in Georgia began flooding the Legislature.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/23/us/politics/23gopvoting0/merlin_184534842_cf5d02a2