Xi, also a co-writer) is an actress brutalized and exploited by a misogynist film industry, and the Taiwanese director, Midi Z, never pulls his punches. Yet this startlingly evocative, complex and confrontational new film is not interested in justice or didacticism.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/arts/ninawu1/merlin_185262843_e4811903-70a1-41b5-b70b-2ea536580ac0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/26/arts/ninawu1/merlin_185262843_e4811903-70a1-41b5-b70b-2ea536580ac0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/arts/ninawu1/merlin_185262843_e4811903-70a1-41b5-b70b-2ea536580ac0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/arts/ninawu1/merlin_185262843_e4811903-70a1-41b5-b70b-2ea536580ac0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/arts/ninawu1/ninawu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/26/arts/ninawu1/ninawu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/arts/ninawu1/ninawu1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Nina Wu’ Review: Destruction of Body and Soul', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Actress Wins a Role, Then the Losses Begin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nina Wu (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Midi Z (Chao Te-yin) (1982- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-25T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beatrice Loayza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beatrice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Loayza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/889c86b2-de49-5523-afd4-0105c982ea88', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/889c86b2-de49-5523-afd4-0105c982ea88'}, {'abstract': 'This Giorgio Serafini movie takes us to a retirement center, a drag race and the DMV, not to mention a dizzying encounter on public transportation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/25/movies/senior-moment-review.html', 'snippet': 'This Giorgio Serafini movie takes us to a retirement center, a drag race and the DMV, not to mention a dizzying encounter on public transportation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many here among us for whom the prospect of spending 90 minutes in the presence of William Shatner would be unalloyed bliss. The world is a funny place. In any event, for them, “Senior Moment,” a romantic comedy, will be, well, unalloyed bliss.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/25/arts/25SENIOR-MOMENT/merlin_185265423_35619abd-8ec1-4095-8077-0566a3ae1e16-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': '