arnaz Fassihi and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kingsley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ronen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Farnaz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fassihi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54b541e3-9667-5bac-a37f-362f67a1f600', 'word_count': 1787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54b541e3-9667-5bac-a37f-362f67a1f600'}, {'abstract': 'Was it the unfortunate use of a single word? Or something far more complicated?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/26/nyregion/CUNY-law-school-mary-lu-bilek-racism.html', 'snippet': 'Was it the unfortunate use of a single word? Or something far more complicated?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the afternoon of Saturday, March 20, Mary Lu Bilek, who has spent 32 years at the law school at the City University of New York, the past five of them as dean, sent an email to students and faculty with the subject line: “Apology.” Ms. Bilek, who is 65, was explaining why she had cryptically announced her retirement two months earlier and why she expected now to leave even sooner. Discussing a contentious issue of race and tenure in a committee meeting last fall, she had likened herself to a “slaveholder.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/nyregion/26big/26big-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy