ch 26 episode of “The Ezra Klein Show.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Tuesday and Friday, Ezra Klein invites you into a conversation about something that matters, like today’s episode with Kristen Soltis Anderson. Listen wherever you get your podcasts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transcript: Ezra Klein Interviews Kristen Soltis Anderson', 'kicker': 'The Ezra Klein Show', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-03-26T12:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0766504a-2146-5973-8c6d-c35428a6220c', 'word_count': 11882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0766504a-2146-5973-8c6d-c35428a6220c'}, {'abstract': 'Alex Rodriguez isn’t like the other athletes getting into blank-check firms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/26/business/dealbook/spac-sports-arod.html', 'snippet': 'Alex Rodriguez isn’t like the other athletes getting into blank-check firms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Professional athletes can sell almost anything, from soda to sneakers to car insurance. But lately they’ve used their star power to sell SPACs, the blank-check acquisition vehicles that have raised more than $90 billion this year. Amid frenzied competition for merger deals, about a fifth of SPACs launched since last year have brought athletes on board in hopes of standing out when pitching to start-ups they hope to take public, Matthew Goldstein and DealBook’s Lauren Hirsch report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/business/26db-arod/merlin_110828089_6779255f-a6be-4e70-b566-0e1af2954eb7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/26/business/26db-arod/merlin_110828089_6779255f-a6be-4e70-b566-0e1af2954eb7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/business/26db-arod/merlin_110828089_6779255f-a6be-4e70-b566-0e1af2954eb7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/business/26db-arod/merlin_110828089_6779255f-a6be-4e70-b566-0e1af2954eb7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/business/26db-arod/merlin_110828089_6779255f-a6be-4e70-b566-0e1af2954eb7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/26/business/26db-arod/merlin_110828089_6779255f-a6be-4e70-b566-0e1af2954eb7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/26/business/26db-arod/merlin_110828089_6779255f-a6be-4e70-b566-0e1af2954eb7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Sports and SPACs', 'kicker': 'DealBook Newsletter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-26T12:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'art