ex, which includes a Metro stop on the downtown-bound Red Line.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/realestate/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/29/realestate/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/realestate/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/realestate/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/realestate/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/29/realestate/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/realestate/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA/29WYG-CA-slide-NMNA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '$1.1 Million Homes in California', 'kicker': 'What you Get', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santa Clara (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-26T21:14:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Angela Serratore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Angela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Serratore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3271a3c2-28ed-5640-a105-9a77afd353fc', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3271a3c2-28ed-5640-a105-9a77afd353fc'}, {'abstract': 'Regaining what the coronavirus took from you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/26/podcasts/coronavirus-smell-testing-loss.html', 'snippet': 'Regaining what the coronavirus took from you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hi everyone, phew, we made it to Friday. There was some heaviness in our coverage this week — including some of the neurological symptoms of long-Covid and the King Soopers shooting in Colorado. In between, we tried to splice in some brightness: the prospect of widespread vaccination and a nursing home’s first day out of lockdown. To keep the optimism going, we’d love to hear what you’re most looking forward to in a post-vaccination future. Shoot us an email and we might share your update in a future newsletter. (And if you’re still questioning whether a vaccine is for you, take a look at this guide answering your questions about vaccine safety and access.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/03/dining/26daily-nl-2/02smell3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge'