eran of the bench in Hennepin County, ordered that the trial be televised, a first in Minnesota.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judge Peter A. Cahill is a 14-year veteran of the bench in Hennepin County. He has previously worked as a public defender, private defense lawyer and prosecutor, rising to become chief deputy under Amy Klobuchar, now a U.S. senator, when she served as the county attorney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/multimedia/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge/merlin_185722578_163d78cc-f510-422f-8096-07f467d9ea0d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/29/multimedia/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge/merlin_185722578_163d78cc-f510-422f-8096-07f467d9ea0d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/multimedia/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge/merlin_185722578_163d78cc-f510-422f-8096-07f467d9ea0d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/multimedia/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge/merlin_185722578_163d78cc-f510-422f-8096-07f467d9ea0d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/multimedia/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/29/multimedia/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/29/multimedia/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge/29briefing-chauvin-trial-judge-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What we know about the judge in the Derek Chauvin trial.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Floyd, George (d 2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chauvin, Derek (1976- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-29T19:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ff80087-9543-597e-9f72-570c45464658', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ff80087-9543-597e-9f72-570c45464658'}, {'abstract': 'Vanessa Seder’s new book, “Eat Cool,” focuses on recipes that require minimal oven and stove use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/dining/eat-cool-cookbook.html', 'snippet': 'Vanessa Seder’s new book, “Eat Cool,” focuses on recipes that require minimal oven and stove use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it rushing things to recommend a cookbook based largely on alluring dishes that are prepped and assembled, but mostly uncooked or barely so? It’s spring,  after all, and the incentive to prepare salads instead of stews is compelling. Vanessa Seder, the author of “Eat Cool,” is a chef and writer  in Portland, Maine, who suggests recipes like a platter of judiciously spiced melon and cucumbers, scallop ceviche and an inviting array of tinned seafood. Other ideas include a green shakshuka, quick pasta with crab and chiles, a glass-noodle salad with lemongrass, fish sauce and seared ground pork, and a page of ideas for using a purchased rotisserie chicken. She has you use a stove and oven here and there, but not for a fruit pie because, as she explained in an email, baking a tart really heats up the kitchen. Instead, among her desserts is an intriguingly refreshing lemon semifreddo made with salted preserved lemons.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-book/29burner-book--articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-book/29burner-book--articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 742}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-book/29burner-book--jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 829, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-book/29burner-book--superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1658, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-book/29burner-book--thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-book/29burner-book--thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-book/29burner-book--thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cookbook to Plan for Summer', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Prepare: If You Can’t Take the Heat, Use This Cookbook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Me)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-29T19:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f4246b-3ad6-5af1-9cbe-b383d21907e4', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f4246b-3ad6-5af1-9cbe-b383d21907e4'}, {'abstract': 'Sugar Hill Creamery’s new blueberry confection is available at its Harlem and Hamilton Heights shops, and nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/dining/cheesecake-sugar-hill-creamery.html', 'snippet': 'Sugar Hill Creamery’s new blueberry confection is available at its Harlem and Hamilton Heights shops, and nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back when we had a share in a ski house at Mount Snow, Vt., we’d drive up with a cheesecake in the trunk of the car. It was frozen by the time we reached our destination and delicious to eat without thawing. The new blueberry ice cream cheesecake that Nicholas Larsen and Petrushka Bazin Larsen have introduced at their Sugar Hill Creamery in Harlem evoked that taste memory. Theirs is not a cheesecake, strictly speaking: It is made from ice cream that has a cream-cheese base, set on a spiced graham cracker crust with a topping of blueberry gelée. Remove it from the freezer about 10 minutes before serving. Fresh blueberries lightly stewed in a little maple syrup are excellent alongside.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-cake/29burner-cake-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-cake/29burner-cake-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-cake/29burner-cake-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-cake/29burner-cake-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-cake/29burner-cake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-cake/29burner-cake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-cake/29burner-cake-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Cheesecake Evokes Memories', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Indulge: An Ice Cream Cheesecake That Evokes Memories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheesecake', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Cream and Frozen Desserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blueberries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sugar Hill Creamery (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-29T19:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0d1326a-5bee-56b8-9580-18bf3fb1a4e6', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0d1326a-5bee-56b8-9580-18bf3fb1a4e6'}, {'abstract': 'The blue and white dishes are made by Janet Belden, a potter in Long Island City, Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/dining/m-wells-cassoulet-bowls.html', 'snippet': 'The blue and white dishes are made by Janet Belden, a potter in Long Island City, Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cassoulet season has ended, but the handmade bowls that M. Wells in Long Island City, Queens, commissioned to bake and serve theirs this year are timeless. The blue-and-white pottery pieces, in slightly varied designs and tones, can just as easily hold servings of bouillabaisse or be used for summer berries, cherries, a thatch of coleslaw or crudités. They’re made by Janet Belden, a local potter, with a Majolica-style glaze, and they are oven and microwave-safe. Each is about eight inches in diameter with a capacity just shy of a quart. You might start to think about Mother’s Day.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-dish1/29burner-dish1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-dish1/29burner-dish1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-dish1/29burner-dish1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-dish1/29burner-dish1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-dish1/29burner-dish1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-dish1/29burner-dish1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-dish1/29burner-dish1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'M. Wells Offers Its Cassoulet Bowls', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Fill: M. Wells Offers  Its Cassoulet Bowls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-29T20:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f98dc5d5-1584-5932-9cdb-f47ea35bdd8c', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f98dc5d5-1584-5932-9cdb-f47ea35bdd8c'}, {'abstract': 'Dirty Sue’s latest creation features all the spices you need for a strong eye-opener, but none of the tomato juice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/dining/bloody-mary-mix.html', 'snippet': 'Dirty Sue’s latest creation features all the spices you need for a strong eye-opener, but none of the tomato juice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric “E.T.” Tecosky, the Los Angeles bartender behind the line of Dirty Sue cocktail condiments, has come up with a clever new product: a Bloody Mary mix with no tomato juice. Anyone can add tomato juice; Mr. Tecosky’s focus is the spices needed, in addition to his company’s own olive juice, to make a great drink. Each 16-ounce bottle contains enough spice solution for 21 to 32 drinks, according to taste. It’s also a terrific seasoning for gazpacho and steamed clams.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Mary/merlin_185156181_44cbd88a-5b4a-404e-87e1-dcfa799c3d93-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Mary/merlin_185156181_44cbd88a-5b4a-404e-87e1-dcfa799c3d93-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Mary/merlin_185156181_44cbd88a-5b4a-404e-87e1-dcfa799c3d93-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Mary/merlin_185156181_44cbd88a-5b4a-404e-87e1-dcfa799c3d93-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Mary/merlin_185156181_44cbd88a-5b4a-404e-87e1-dcfa799c3d93-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Mary/merlin_185156181_44cbd88a-5b4a-404e-87e1-dcfa799c3d93-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Mary/merlin_185156181_44cbd88a-5b4a-404e-87e1-dcfa799c3d93-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloody Mary Mix, Hold the Tomatoes', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Mix: Bloody Mary Mix,  Hold the Tomatoes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails and Mixed Drinks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-29T20:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de897c78-c53c-5ebc-8380-92ee69cbad47', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de897c78-c53c-5ebc-8380-92ee69cbad47'}, {'abstract': 'Utopihen Farms offers six-packs duck eggs — large and golden yolked — nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/dining/duck-eggs-easter.html', 'snippet': 'Utopihen Farms offers six-packs duck eggs — large and golden yolked — nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Duck eggs, larger than hen eggs and containing bigger, deep golden yolks and a larger proportion of protein-rich whites, are sold at some farmers’ markets. Now Utopihen Farms has started selling the duck eggs nationally, raised on a group of small family farms with a home base in New Holland, Pa. Their duck (and chicken) eggs are from birds that forage in fields, and are given the title “pasture-raised.” The richness and size of the eggs are what make them so excellent scrambled, fried, poached, in omelets or however you like them. For baking you’ll need to adjust a recipe: The general rule is two duck eggs for three large chicken eggs. And for coloring and decorating for Easter, the eggs provide a larger canvas for your artwork, and they have thicker shells, too.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Duck/29burner-Duck-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Duck/29burner-Duck-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Duck/29burner-Duck-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Duck/29burner-Duck-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1442, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Duck/29burner-Duck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Duck/29burner-Duck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-Duck/29burner-Duck-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Larger Canvas for Your Easter Egg', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Enrich: A Larger Canvas For Your Easter Egg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ducks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-29T20:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/126239c4-caa9-52b1-afab-5a029c1eb3de', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/126239c4-caa9-52b1-afab-5a029c1eb3de'}, {'abstract': 'The pastry chef Ron Paprocki has added colorful filled confections for springtime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/dining/gotham-bar-and-grill-chocolate.html', 'snippet': 'The pastry chef Ron Paprocki has added colorful filled confections for springtime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gotham Bar & Grill has been closed for a little over a year (with plans to reopen this summer), but that hasn’t stopped the pastry chef Ron Paprocki from continuing to turn out his chocolate treats. For spring this year, there are pastel bonbons filled with passion fruit caramel, lemon olive oil and raspberry ganache. They come nestled in a gift box.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-goth2/merlin_185770881_972c7985-ada5-4579-a0cb-a9a2ecddfd9e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-goth2/merlin_185770881_972c7985-ada5-4579-a0cb-a9a2ecddfd9e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-goth2/merlin_185770881_972c7985-ada5-4579-a0cb-a9a2ecddfd9e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-goth2/merlin_185770881_972c7985-ada5-4579-a0cb-a9a2ecddfd9e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-goth2/merlin_185770881_972c7985-ada5-4579-a0cb-a9a2ecddfd9e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-goth2/merlin_185770881_972c7985-ada5-4579-a0cb-a9a2ecddfd9e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/dining/29burner-goth2/merlin_185770881_972c7985-ada5-4579-a0cb-a9a2ecddfd9e-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chocolate Bonbon Worthy of Gotham', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Nibble: A Chocolate Bonbon  Worthy of Gotham', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-29T20:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1fa03fd-b452-523a-a85b-a9e50dc6b9e5', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1fa03fd-b452-523a-a85b-a9e50dc6b9e5'}, {'abstract': 'Keli Goff’s series of vignettes feature Black women recounting how their hair affected their school lives, relationships or careers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/theater/crowns-kinks-and-curls-review.html', 'snippet': 'Keli Goff’s series of vignettes feature Black women recounting how their hair affected their school lives, relationships or careers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have 4b hair that remained virgin hair, mostly styled in box braids and cornrows with extensions, until I was 13, when I got my first relaxer. My scalp has known chemical burns, hot comb burns, curling iron burns, flat iron burns and the unrelenting throbbing that comes wi