rson': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Margolies', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46bb7988-f265-5197-9b2b-efd509d3980b', 'word_count': 1264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46bb7988-f265-5197-9b2b-efd509d3980b'}, {'abstract': 'The Crescent City is the kind of place you daydream about long after you’re gone. Here are a few ways to be there in spirit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/30/travel/new-orleans-vacation-at-home.html', 'snippet': 'The Crescent City is the kind of place you daydream about long after you’re gone. Here are a few ways to be there in spirit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the course of the decade since I first visited, I have often imagined myself at home in New Orleans. I think of the syncopated shuffle of a snare drum, the simple pleasure of an afternoon walk with a to-go beer in hand and the candy-colored shotgun houses that sink into the ground at odd angles. And so it wasn’t a huge surprise when, at the beginning of 2021, I found myself packing up my life and moving to the Crescent City for a few months. Why not be somewhere I love at this difficult time, I thought? Why not live in my daydreams for a little while?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/multimedia/00aroundworld-nola-top/00aroundworld-nola-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/multimedia/00aroundworld-nola-top/00aroundworld-nola-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/multimedia/00aroundworld-nola-top/00aroundworld-nola-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'j