://article/8601d853-7d79-5631-9464-97b73056a534'}, {'abstract': 'For a forensic cleaner in Mexico City, helping grieving families heal is at the core of his service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/30/opinion/the-death-cleaner-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'For a forensic cleaner in Mexico City, helping grieving families heal is at the core of his service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Death is Donovan Tavera’s business. For nearly 20 years, Tavera has been a forensic cleaner in Mexico City, providing families of the deceased with the solace of a clean home. For mourning families, his services become integral to their healing process. The short documentary above, filmed before the pandemic, considers what it means to wash away what’s left after someone dies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Death Cleaner', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-30T19:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/141e4431-8266-565c-a253-5b05f9869cc4', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141e4431-8266-565c-a253-5b05f9869cc4'}, {'abstract': 'Readers propose research to address police killings of civilians. Also: Why menthol cigarettes should be banned; The Nation magazine’s history; the Republicans’ problem; museum fi