rs is a concern.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/31/upshot/how-food-banks-succeeded-and-what-they-need-now.html', 'snippet': 'Fatigue among donors and workers is a concern.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'The people who run America’s charitable food banks take pride in what they’ve accomplished over the past year, and the numbers justify it: They distributed roughly 50 percent more food in 2020 compared with 2019, a considerable portion to first-time visitors. They served millions of people even as they dealt with supply-chain interruptions and health risks for their volunteers and employees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Food Banks Succeeded and What They Need Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Banks and Pantries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Insecurity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Risks and Safety Concerns', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Feeding America', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-31T09:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alicia Parlapiano, Quoctrung Bui and Lucy Hewett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alicia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parlapiano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Quoctrung', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bui', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization':