ge Floyd’s family and one for Mr. Chauvin’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the courtroom, a rotating pool of journalists is monitoring the action.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chauvin, Derek (1976- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-03-31T15:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Fazio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fazio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e47dc4-f4c7-5435-8eab-603c82b597bd', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e47dc4-f4c7-5435-8eab-603c82b597bd'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Mario Draghi issued a decree requiring that workers in health care facilities be vaccinated, a move that will test the legal limits of his government’s efforts to stem coronavirus outbreaks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/31/world/europe/italy-covid-vaccines-health-workers.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Mario Draghi issued a decree requiring that workers in health care facilities be vaccinated, a move that will test the legal limits of his government’s efforts to stem coronavirus outbreaks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Giulio Macciò tested negative for the coronavirus and spent weeks receiving treatment for emphysema in a sealed-off hospital under the care of doctors and lung specialists —\xa0and a nurse who had refused to be vaccinated. On March 11, he unexpectedly died. A post-mortem swab found that he had contracted the virus, as had 14 other patients and the unvaccinated nurse who spent her shifts in his midst.', 'source': 'The New York Time